## Set a car''s rates and kilometres

Open the car, then the **Rates** tab. Everything on it saves together, in one step.

1. Type the four rates. Only the daily rate is needed: an empty weekend rate is the daily rate, an empty weekly rate is 6 days at the daily rate, and an empty monthly rate is 22 days.
2. Kilometres: keep **Use the defaults** (the kilometres a day in Settings, Kilometre choices, and the extra kilometre rate in Fee defaults for the car''s class), or choose **Custom for this car** and type them.
3. Check the deposit (the class default is filled in), and the delivery and pickup fees: each is one way, an empty pickup fee is the delivery fee, and 0 means not offered.
4. Read What renters pay under the fields: real prices for a weekend, a few weekdays, a week and a month, worked out the way bookings are priced. Press **Save the rates**.

| Rate | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Daily rate | A price per day, for each day that starts on a Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday |
| Weekend rate | A price per day, not for the whole weekend: each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday. Friday 10 am to Sunday 10 am is 2 days at this rate; Sunday to Monday is a daily day |
| Weekly rate | The price for 7 days. Rentals of 7 to 29 days cost this for each 7 days, counted by the day. A 1 to 6 day rental never costs more |
| Monthly rate | The price for 30 days. A 7 to 29 day rental never costs more |

5. Lead-time pricing for this car, below the rates: **Program settings** (the tiers there), **Off for this car**, or **Its own tiers** (a table like the one in Program settings). Press **Save**.

> Tip: A problem shows on its own field, in words, as you type. When similar cars have rates, a line suggests them with Use these; it is only a hint. The same fields are on **Add a car**, so a car can be added with its rates in one pass.

## Fleet tracking

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, the **Fleet tracking** tab. Fleet staff have the same map as **Fleet map** in their menu, and field staff see the cars of their own jobs under **Map**. Every car on the same map as the Live map, with who has it. Positions are seen by Admins and fleet staff only.

1. The four numbers: cars on rent, moving, parked, and open alerts.
2. The map shows each car as its photo in a ring: green moving (the arrow is its heading), yellow engine on, blue parked, orange not reporting. The list beside it has every car with its renter, booking, when it is due back (late in red) and its state.
3. Press a car on the map or in the list for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery, whether the tracker has the car''s power, and the trip under way.
4. **Alerts**: speeding, left Ontario, left your zone, still driving after the return time, low tracker battery, unplugged and not reporting. Each also comes to the bell and, with phone alerts on, under Urgent alerts. Press **Show** to see where, **Seen** when it is handled, or **Mark all as seen**.
5. **Trips by booking**: each booking''s trips, kilometres and top speed (red at the speeding level). Press the last trip to draw its route on the map.

## Pair a tracker with a car

1. A new tracker that reports shows under **Trackers**, "Reporting, not on a car yet". Press **Pair**, choose the car and the install date.
2. Or press **Pair a tracker** and type its device ID (the IMEI or serial number on the tracker).
3. The install date starts the Tracker Fee on the owner''s invoice when the car has none yet. A replacement tracker keeps the car''s first date; the old tracker is taken off by itself.
4. **Remove** takes a tracker off a car (tick "faulty" for a broken one). The Tracker Fee is not changed.

## Tracking settings

Below the trackers: the speeding level (140 km/h), the minutes of grace after the return time (15), the low battery level (20%), the hours before "not reporting" (6), the Ontario alert, and one optional zone (a name, its centre and a radius in km). History keeps a moving car''s position once a minute for 90 days, trips and alerts for 365 days (at most 365: the privacy policy keeps tracker data 12 months).

1. Demo mode (off): simulated cars drive the GTA''s highways here and on the Live map, for a demonstration. Nothing is saved. Turn it off before the trackers go live.
2. **Make the ingest key**: the relay or tracker service signs every batch of positions with it. It is shown once; making a new one stops the old one at once.

> Tip: The Live map shows the same cars with its Fleet layer (tick Fleet).

## The listing pipeline

Open **Cars** > **Listings**. A draft waiting for review shows Needs review.

1. Each row shows the car, plate, state, photos and the work done on it so far.
2. Press **Start a listing** to begin one for a car that has none.
3. Open a car to review it.

![](/guides/img/admin-09-listings-desktop-970819b6.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings; pins: 1 53.5 37.0, 2 87.2 21.1, 3 32.6 37.0")

## Review a listing

1. Steps to go live shows four numbered steps: **1 Photos** (how many of the required photos are in, 14 for most cars, 13 for a two-seater with no rear seats), **2 Cover plates**, **3 Review** and **4 Live on the site**. Each says what it needs and has one button to where it is done; the step to do now is in red. A step that stopped (a photo edit or the copy) shows under them with **Retry**.
2. Similar cars on file lists possible duplicates. Press **Not a duplicate** or **Same car**. An open flag does not keep the car off the site; only Same car does.
3. The copy is written by itself from the car''s facts and published when it passes the checks: nothing to type. To change a line, press Change; that field is then locked and kept by every new version.
4. Under Photos, each public photo shows its plate state: Plate not checked, Plate covered or No plate visible.

![](/guides/img/admin-10-listing-review-desktop-352745fd.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1100; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449; pins: 1 20.6 16.6, 2 86.1 47.5, 3 19.9 106.8, 4 74.9 106.8")

## Cover the licence plate

On each public photo press **Cover the plate**. The editor opens.

1. The box over the plate is already suggested: as soon as the review opens, every outside photo (the More outside photos included) gets its suggestion, and those photos show Box suggested. Check it. **Suggest the plate** asks again.
2. Drag over a plate to draw a box. Drag a box to move it, or its corner to resize it.
3. Under Cover the plate with, keep **The CARMA Ontario plate** (on a rear plate: the company''s own Ontario plate CARMA, drawn in the photo''s perspective and light) or **Edit the front plate out** (on a front photo: the bumper is filled in, no box), or choose **A CarmaCars plate**, **Pixelation** or **Blur**. Photos covered the old way are made again the new way by themselves.
4. Press **Save the covered photo**. **Clear the boxes** starts over.
5. No plate in the shot? Press **No plate visible on this photo**.

![](/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-desktop-4219ad93.jpg "desktop; size: 690 703; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449; pins: 1 42.5 83.8, 2 49.6 29.9, 3 4.3 77.4, 4 15.5 83.8, 5 18.1 91.2")

> Tip: The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately. Keyboard: N adds a box, the arrows move it, Shift and the arrows resize it, Delete removes it.

## Publish

1. A real car that is not on the site is a line on To do: press **Set rates and publish**. The daily rate is filled in (the car''s own, or the suggested rate from similar cars or the class); change it if you like and press **Publish now**.
2. On the car itself, the Listing tab has **Publish now**; each open item of its checklist has a button to where it is done.
3. From a listing review: press **Approve and publish**, **Approve, publish later**, or **Send back** with what to fix.

> Watch out: The plate check never holds a car back: a real photo whose plate is not checked stays private (the other photos, or the sample photos, show instead) and goes public by itself once its plate is covered or marked not visible. Listings already live show "Plate not checked" on such photos.

## Photos filed under the wrong shot, and interior windows

1. On the Photos card, each shot lists its photos. A photo filed under the wrong shot: press **Remove** under it, then **Remove it**. The shot is free again: take or pick the right photo. The removed photo is kept privately and the removal is in the history. A live listing''s photos change in the review instead (Reject).
2. Dashboard and seat photos: what shows through the windows is replaced by the studio background when the cut is clean (a quality check: some but not most of the frame seen through, high in the frame, a few clean regions, sharp edges). Otherwise the windows are blurred, and the photo is marked windows blurred. Nothing to do.
3. A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.

## A listing without photos yet: sample photos

A car can be listed before its photos are taken. Until then the site shows a sample photo.

1. Submit the listing without photos. The listing copy is still written for you from the car''s details.
2. The car page and the car''s card show a sample photo, captioned "Sample photo", so renters know it is not this car. Staff see "Using sample photos" on the car and in Listings.
3. Publishing does not wait for a plate check: a sample photo has no plate.
4. Add the real photos when they are taken. Once real photos are approved they replace the sample at once; nothing else to do.

## Sample photos

**Settings** > **Sample photos**. The pictures a car shows until its real photos are in.

1. Every body type has a built-in picture (sedan, SUV, truck, van, coupe, hatchback, electric car).
2. Add your own: choose the Body type, and a Make and Model if the photo is of that exact model, pick the Photo, and press **Add the photo**.
3. The most specific photo wins: make and model, then make and body type, then body type. **Turn off** or **Delete** a photo you no longer want.
4. Cars using sample photos lists the cars still waiting for real photos. Each real car showing sample photos is also a line on To do, with **Add photos**.

![](/guides/img/admin-36-sample-photos-desktop-55c64070.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 812; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings/sample-photos; pins: 4 26.8 28.9")

## Publish now, and new cars published by themselves

Nothing between a new car and the site has to be finished first: the car goes on the site, and what is still open shows on its checklist.

1. **Settings** > **Program**, **Publish new cars automatically** (on by default): a new real car goes on the site by itself as soon as it has its year, make and model and its rates, when it is added with rates, when its rates are saved, when it is added for an owner, or when an owner''s application is approved.
2. Otherwise open the car: its Listing tab says why it is not on the site and has **Publish now**. A car with no rates yet is published with the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults in Program settings); change them later on the Rates tab.
3. Every real car has its listing from the moment it is added, as a draft. It shows in Listings and in Not on the site yet until it is published.
4. An owner''s own application waits for your decision before its car is published by itself; Publish now still works.
5. A car taken off the site by staff, or scheduled for a later date, is never published by itself: press **Publish now**.

## The checklist: what is still open on a listed car

Open items never stop publishing. They show as warnings on the car''s Listing tab and after Publish now.

| Item | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Paperwork | Ownership permit, registry forms, agreements signed, Forms C and D, upfront payment, registry visit, tracker, safety certificate |
| Insurance | Not on the fleet insurance policy yet: the car can be booked, but not handed over |
| Details | Colour, body, seats, gearbox: the car page leaves out what is missing |
| Photos | No real photos: sample photos stand in. A photo whose plate is not checked stays private until it is |
| No VIN yet | A car added by its plate alone: add the VIN when you have it |
| Possible duplicate | An open flag in Similar cars. Only Same car keeps the car off the site |
| Owner terms | The management fee (Revenue Share) and fees not set: a request uses the owner''s terms or the standard grid |

## The fleet policy rule at handover

A program owner''s car is listed and can be requested, offered and paid for while its paperwork is open. It is never handed over until the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet insurance policy.

- Staff see a warning on a request and an offer for a car not on the policy yet.
- The handover refuses the car until the insurer''s confirmation is recorded (Owners and onboarding). The field app says so on the job.
- Only real states keep a car off the site: retired, left the program, out of service, Turo only, bookings turned off, a self-managed owner in arrears, or a paused listing.

## Cars on sample photos

**Cars**, **Listings** ends with **Cars on sample photos**: each real car whose page still shows sample photos, with its newest handover photos (the check-in and check-out photos field staff take).

1. Where a handover photographed the car, press **Use the handover photos**. They go into the car''s listing as if taken on the capture screen.
2. When every required shot is there, the listing is submitted: the studio editor puts the car on the CarmaCars backdrop, then the listing waits for your review like any other.
3. A car with no handover photos yet gets them at its next handover, or press **Start a listing** and take them.

> Good to know: The studio editor uses Cloudflare image transformations (5,000 a month included). Settings > Usage counts them.

## A car''s registration and documents

Open the car, then **Owner & documents**. The **Registration** card:

1. Correct the **VIN** (it is checked: 17 characters, the check digit, not on another car; decoded again for the body style and trim), the **Year** and the **Body style**.
2. Type the **Ontario permit number** and the date the **Plate sticker expires**. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before; save the new date after the renewal and the task closes.
3. Under **Documents**, choose the kind (**Ownership permit**, Safety Standards Certificate, owner''s insurance, other), pick the photo or PDF and press **Upload**. The ownership permit clears that item of the owner''s checklist.
4. For the **Safety Standards Certificate**, also type its number, the date it was issued and the date it expires. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before it expires; upload the new certificate with its dates and the task closes. It is a document on the car, not a service record, and nothing is billed to the owner.
5. **Add a car** takes the ownership permit and the Safety Standards Certificate too, under **Documents (optional)**.

## A car added under the wrong owner

Open the car, Overview, **Who supplies the car**, **Move to another owner**. Choose the owner, or **CarmaCars (owner not known yet)**: the car becomes a company car, with no owner schedule or terms.

- The car''s unsigned owner application and vehicle schedule are withdrawn (kept in the history), and its draft owner invoices are deleted. Nobody is notified.
- It is refused once anything for the car is signed, issued, paid or on a statement.

### The VIN from the car, not typed

Every VIN field (Add a car, Add a car for an owner, the car''s **Registration**, **Start a listing**) has **Scan the barcode** and **Photo of the VIN**. Scan the barcode in the driver''s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield: the phone''s camera reads it by itself. Or take a photo of the VIN plate or sticker: the barcode in it is read first, else the photo is read for the printed VIN. The VIN is checked (17 characters, the check digit; I, O and Q become 1 and 0) and decoded as when you type it. Check it against the car before saving.

### Photos in any order

**Add photos** on the listing takes any number of photos at once from the camera roll. Each is sorted to its shot by itself (front three-quarter, sides, rear, dashboard, seats and the rest); a shot that already has its photo sends the new one to the extra photos, so nothing is replaced by accident. The shots are a guide, not a rule: a listing is complete with 10 photos that can go on the site and one outside photo for the cover. Outside photos get the studio background: the car is cropped to its edges and placed big in the frame with its wheels on the floor and a soft shadow under the tyres, and any corner watermark or caption beside the car is left out. Inside and detail photos are kept as taken; when one has a watermark, a logo or caption text on it, the edge with the mark is cut off by itself, and a photo whose mark cannot be cut off (one in the middle) stays off the site until you replace it. **Cover the plate** opens on every outside photo with the plate box suggested; check it and save.

Outside photos made before the newest framing (the car small in the frame, or without the model''s name behind it) are made again with **Frame the outside photos again** above the photos of the listing, then **Yes, frame again**. The cover and the main outside views get the model''s name lettered behind the car, as on the sample photos (for example CLA, C CLASS, AMG GT). The photos leave the site until their plates are checked again: the plate box is suggested on the new photos; check each and cover it. On a published listing each goes back on the site once its plate is checked.

## Showroom photos

Outside photos go in the dark CarmaCars showroom by themselves: a simple dark dealership with linear lights in the ceiling, a slatted wood wall between two light strips with a big lit CarmaCars sign, and a polished dark floor with the car''s reflection and a shadow under each tyre. Every angle of a car is in the same room, and the cover has the model''s name in metal letters on the wall under the sign. The image model may relight the car or turn it slightly; a photo that shows another car, model or colour is not used. **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings** has the switch (Showroom photos, on), the image model that makes the photos look photographed, and its daily limit. Past the limit, or when the image model is not available, the site makes the showroom itself for free, and the photo says why under it.

- A car whose photos were made on the black studio: press **Apply showroom to this car** above its photos, then **Yes, apply**.
- Every car at once: **Listings** > **Showroom photos** > **Apply showroom to every car**, then **Yes, every car**.
- Under a photo in the showroom: **Redo** makes it again, **Back to the original** puts back the version before the showroom.

A car that stays where it was keeps its plate check. When the image model made the photo, check the plate again: the photo is off the site until you do. Photos made in the first showroom are made again in the new one with **Apply showroom to this car** or **Apply showroom to every car**.

## Failed photos

The site makes the photo sizes itself: the image service is asked only to cut the car out (**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings**: the switch to let the image service make every photo step is off). When the image service is busy or over its allowance, the photo still goes on the site from the original and is made again later. A listing marked Failed has **Retry failed photos** in its note; **Retry failed photos** at the top does every listing. They are made again a few at a time, and the listing leaves Failed when they are done.

## The first photo: plain, with a model, or a flyer

On a listing, under **First photo**, choose what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit. Switch any time; the other photos stay as they are.

- **Plain car**: the cover photo as it is (the default).
- **With a model**: a car-show photo made by the image model, with a fully clothed adult model beside the car. It needs the image model; until it is made (or when the image model is not there) the plain cover shows, and the listing says why.
- **Flyer**: the cover photo with a band like a printed flyer: the car, the price a day from its live rates, the call to action, a badge and the logo. When the price, the words or the cover photo change, it is made again by itself within 10 minutes; the plain cover shows meanwhile.

**Make it again** makes the chosen one again. The words of the flyer and the description of the model are in **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings** (First photo "flyer" and First photo "with a model"); {car}, {price}, {weekly} and {monthly} are filled for each car.

## Marketing photos in other scenes

For Marketplace and social posts, a car''s outside photos can be made again in other scenes. The website keeps its own photos in the dark showroom: a marketing set never replaces them.

1. On a listing, under **Marketing photos**, choose a scene, or **Mix: a different scene on each photo**, and press **Make the marketing set**.
2. The copies show as they are made. The dark showroom and the plain white studio are made by the site when the image model is not there; the photographic scenes (a bright showroom, a city street at night, the Toronto waterfront, a parking garage, Highway, a scenic road, Brick building) need the image model, and say so on the copy when it is not there.
3. **Download (ZIP)** takes the set; the Marketplace kit''s **With scenes (ZIP)** takes the same set.

**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Marketing scenes** lists the scenes. A scene made in a real place has a photo of that place: Brick building picks its photo by itself: the widest outside photo, as taken, of the shareholders'' own cars. To use another, press **Change the reference photo** and pick one (the shareholders'' cars'' photos come first), or upload one. The scenes'' names and words are in the **Marketing scenes** setting.

## Extra photos

A photo that fits no shot is an extra photo. Under the shots, **Extra outside photos** (put on the studio background) and **Extra inside and detail photos** (touched up) each take any number at once. They count toward the 10 photos, get the same plate check, and come after the standard shots on the car''s page.

1. In the review, **Extra photos, in their order on the car page** lists them.
2. Drag a photo by its handle (⋮⋮), or press **Earlier** or **Later**.
3. Press **Save the order**.

## Fix a cut-out

When the background removal cuts badly (a mirror or a wheel missing, background left beside the car), press **Edit the cut-out** under the outside photo.

1. **Cut-out** shows the car over the photo as taken, shown faintly. Choose **Erase** and brush over what should go, or **Restore** and brush over what the cut-out took off. Set **Brush size** and **Zoom**; when zoomed, **Move the view** pans. **Undo** takes back the last stroke.
2. **On the studio** shows the car on the studio background. Drag the car to move it and use **Size** to make it larger or smaller. **Centre and full size** puts it back.
3. Press **Save as a new version**. The photo is made again in about a minute; the version before and the photo as taken are kept. **Reset to the automatic cut-out** starts again from the automatic one.

> Good to know: If the car did not move, the plate check carries over: a photo marked no plate visible stays so, and a covered plate is covered again on the new photo when the review is open. If the car moved, check the plate again. A photo made before cut-outs were kept shows **Make the cut-out** first; the editor opens by itself when it is ready.

Every photo also gets a light touch-up by itself (exposure, levels, a little contrast and colour, mild sharpening), never enough to change the paint colour or hide a scratch. Turn it off for one photo with **Use original colours** under it (the photo is made again; approve it again), or for every photo in Admin > Settings > **Program settings** (Listings) with **Auto-enhance listing photos**. The photo as uploaded is always kept.
## Import photos from a Google Drive link

The owner often hands over a car''s photos as a public Google Drive folder, or one big folder with a folder per make and then per car. You do not download them: paste the link.

**One car.** On the car''s listing, under the capture, **Import photos from a Google Drive link**. Paste the folder link (shared with Anyone with the link) and press **Import the photos**. Every photo in the folder, and in the folders inside it, is added to this car as if you had pressed Add photos: each is sorted to its shot (else filed as an extra photo, in file-name order), put on the studio background and checked for its plate. The box under the link, **Submit the listing for processing when its photos are in**, is on by default.

**Many cars.** **Cars** > **Import photos from Drive** (a button on Vehicles). Paste the top folder''s link and press **Read the folder**. The page walks every folder and proposes a car for each folder that holds photos, from the year, make, model, colour and plate in the folder names (the make folder above counts; 01 Motors partner cars come first). Check the table: tick or untick **Import**, change the car in the list (the likely cars come first), leave out a folder with **Do not import this folder**. A line marked **Check this one** matched two alike cars. Then press **Import N photos from M folders**.

1. The page follows the import by itself. You can leave it and come back: it runs in the background.
2. The end shows the summary: imported, skipped and failed, and why for each (a file over 15 MB, a file that is not a photo, the same photo already on the car, a folder not shared).
3. **Try the failed photos again** takes only the ones that failed. Pressing Import on the same link again never adds a photo twice: a Drive file already on the car is skipped, and so is the same picture under another name. A photo you took off the car can be imported again.

> Good to know: JPG, PNG, HEIC and WebP only (HEIC and WebP are made JPEG first). At most 15 MB a photo, 600 photos, 400 folders and 4 GB in one import. Drive is asked politely, one photo at a time; a big import takes a while.

> Good to know: Without a key, Drive shows only the first 50 files of a folder on its public page; a folder with more is read in full when Drive allows it. In **Settings**, the **Photo import from Google Drive** box takes a Google API key with the Drive API on (after it is saved only its last 4 characters are shown, and it is never written to the change log): with it, folders of any size are read and photos download without Drive''s warning pages.

## Pickup from owner and return to owner (release 28)

On a car''s page, **Pickup from owner and return to owner** records the car''s condition when CarmaCars picks it up from its owner or gives it back: the date and time, km, fuel, many photos at once with the suggested angles, and notes. **Add photos** adds more to a record later. The owner sees these records read only on the car''s page in their portal. They are the baseline condition for any dispute.

## Incident cards (release 34)
**Cars** > **Vehicles** > **Incident cards** prints the card for each car: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, the support number from Settings, a roadside number when there is one, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. Open a car and press **Incident card** to print only that car; on the list, **Print all cars** prints them all, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks, ready to laminate. Under Fleet insurance policy press **Add the policy** (the insurer, the policy number, the dates, the named insured, the roadside number on the slip) and choose the uploaded slip if you have one: it is printed as it is, otherwise the fields are. The card never shows a premium. Fleet staff print the same cards from their portal.

## Field jobs, shifts and who gets a job

**Cars**, then **Field jobs**, is the board Fleet uses, with every action Fleet has. Field staff take shifts you publish with **Publish shifts**. Jobs go on shifts, not on people: each job is put on the shift covering its time (or that day''s), whoever holds the shift does it (several people share the jobs, least busy first), a shift nobody holds keeps its jobs for whoever claims it, and work lands only on days with shifts (work due on a day without shifts moves to the day before, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day; the booking''s own times never change). A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning on the board and on the booking. **To a shift** moves a job to another shift. You can give a job to a field person on a shift that day or to an Admin, take it off with **Unassign** (tick **Tell them** to let them know), and an Admin who holds a job opens it on the field portal. A person who has not passed the academy cannot be given a job or take a shift. A shift with jobs and nobody on it within 24 hours alerts Fleet and the Admins once.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Vehicles is the fleet. Listings turns a car into a page on carmacars.ca in four steps: photos, covered plates, a review, and live on the site.</p><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-vehicles" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Vehicles</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b></p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by status; More filters has who supplies the car, retired cars and the mode. Each row shows the plate, class, owner, mode, status, listing and daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Search by plate, model or owner. <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Rates for many cars</b> changes the rates of many cars at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a car for its tabs: Overview, Rates, Fees and coverage, Calendar, Listing, and Owner, documents, tracker. The Tracker card links to Fleet tracking.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/900"><img src="/guides/img/admin-08-vehicles-desktop-46461f49.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="900"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.3%;top:31.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:37.5%;top:24.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:48.6%;top:52.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-set-a-car-s-rates-and-kilometres" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Set a car&#39;s rates and kilometres</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, then the <b class="gd-ui">Rates</b> tab. Everything on it saves together, in one step.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type the four rates. Only the daily rate is needed: an empty weekend rate is the daily rate, an empty weekly rate is 6 days at the daily rate, and an empty monthly rate is 22 days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Kilometres: keep <b class="gd-ui">Use the defaults</b> (the kilometres a day in Settings, Kilometre choices, and the extra kilometre rate in Fee defaults for the car&#39;s class), or choose <b class="gd-ui">Custom for this car</b> and type them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check the deposit (the class default is filled in), and the delivery and pickup fees: each is one way, an empty pickup fee is the delivery fee, and 0 means not offered.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Read What renters pay under the fields: real prices for a weekend, a few weekdays, a week and a month, worked out the way bookings are priced. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rates</b>.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Rate</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Daily rate</td><td>A price per day, for each day that starts on a Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday</td></tr><tr><td>Weekend rate</td><td>A price per day, not for the whole weekend: each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday. Friday 10 am to Sunday 10 am is 2 days at this rate; Sunday to Monday is a daily day</td></tr><tr><td>Weekly rate</td><td>The price for 7 days. Rentals of 7 to 29 days cost this for each 7 days, counted by the day. A 1 to 6 day rental never costs more</td></tr><tr><td>Monthly rate</td><td>The price for 30 days. A 7 to 29 day rental never costs more</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol" start="5"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Lead-time pricing for this car, below the rates: <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> (the tiers there), <b class="gd-ui">Off for this car</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Its own tiers</b> (a table like the one in Program settings). Press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A problem shows on its own field, in words, as you type. When similar cars have rates, a line suggests them with Use these; it is only a hint. The same fields are on <b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b>, so a car can be added with its rates in one pass.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-fleet-tracking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fleet tracking</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Fleet tracking</b> tab. Fleet staff have the same map as <b class="gd-ui">Fleet map</b> in their menu, and field staff see the cars of their own jobs under <b class="gd-ui">Map</b>. Every car on the same map as the Live map, with who has it. Positions are seen by Admins and fleet staff only.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The four numbers: cars on rent, moving, parked, and open alerts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The map shows each car as its photo in a ring: green moving (the arrow is its heading), yellow engine on, blue parked, orange not reporting. The list beside it has every car with its renter, booking, when it is due back (late in red) and its state.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press a car on the map or in the list for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery, whether the tracker has the car&#39;s power, and the trip under way.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b>: speeding, left Ontario, left your zone, still driving after the return time, low tracker battery, unplugged and not reporting. Each also comes to the bell and, with phone alerts on, under Urgent alerts. Press <b class="gd-ui">Show</b> to see where, <b class="gd-ui">Seen</b> when it is handled, or <b class="gd-ui">Mark all as seen</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Trips by booking</b>: each booking&#39;s trips, kilometres and top speed (red at the speeding level). Press the last trip to draw its route on the map.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-pair-a-tracker-with-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pair a tracker with a car</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A new tracker that reports shows under <b class="gd-ui">Trackers</b>, &quot;Reporting, not on a car yet&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Pair</b>, choose the car and the install date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Or press <b class="gd-ui">Pair a tracker</b> and type its device ID (the IMEI or serial number on the tracker).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The install date starts the Tracker Fee on the owner&#39;s invoice when the car has none yet. A replacement tracker keeps the car&#39;s first date; the old tracker is taken off by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes a tracker off a car (tick &quot;faulty&quot; for a broken one). The Tracker Fee is not changed.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-tracking-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tracking settings</h2><p class="gd-p">Below the trackers: the speeding level (140 km/h), the minutes of grace after the return time (15), the low battery level (20%), the hours before &quot;not reporting&quot; (6), the Ontario alert, and one optional zone (a name, its centre and a radius in km). History keeps a moving car&#39;s position once a minute for 90 days, trips and alerts for 365 days (at most 365: the privacy policy keeps tracker data 12 months).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Demo mode (off): simulated cars drive the GTA&#39;s highways here and on the Live map, for a demonstration. Nothing is saved. Turn it off before the trackers go live.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Make the ingest key</b>: the relay or tracker service signs every batch of positions with it. It is shown once; making a new one stops the old one at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The Live map shows the same cars with its Fleet layer (tick Fleet).</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-listing-pipeline" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The listing pipeline</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>. A draft waiting for review shows Needs review.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each row shows the car, plate, state, photos and the work done on it so far.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> to begin one for a car that has none.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a car to review it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-09-listings-desktop-970819b6.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:53.5%;top:37%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:87.2%;top:21.1%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:32.6%;top:37%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-review-a-listing" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review a listing</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Steps to go live shows four numbered steps: <b class="gd-ui">1 Photos</b> (how many of the required photos are in, 14 for most cars, 13 for a two-seater with no rear seats), <b class="gd-ui">2 Cover plates</b>, <b class="gd-ui">3 Review</b> and <b class="gd-ui">4 Live on the site</b>. Each says what it needs and has one button to where it is done; the step to do now is in red. A step that stopped (a photo edit or the copy) shows under them with <b class="gd-ui">Retry</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Similar cars on file lists possible duplicates. Press <b class="gd-ui">Not a duplicate</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Same car</b>. An open flag does not keep the car off the site; only Same car does.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The copy is written by itself from the car&#39;s facts and published when it passes the checks: nothing to type. To change a line, press Change; that field is then locked and kept by every new version.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Under Photos, each public photo shows its plate state: Plate not checked, Plate covered or No plate visible.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1100"><img src="/guides/img/admin-10-listing-review-desktop-352745fd.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1100"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.6%;top:16.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:86.1%;top:47.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.9%;top:100%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.9%;top:100%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-cover-the-licence-plate" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cover the licence plate</h2><p class="gd-p">On each public photo press <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b>. The editor opens.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The box over the plate is already suggested: as soon as the review opens, every outside photo (the More outside photos included) gets its suggestion, and those photos show Box suggested. Check it. <b class="gd-ui">Suggest the plate</b> asks again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Drag over a plate to draw a box. Drag a box to move it, or its corner to resize it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under Cover the plate with, keep <b class="gd-ui">The CARMA Ontario plate</b> (on a rear plate: the company&#39;s own Ontario plate CARMA, drawn in the photo&#39;s perspective and light) or <b class="gd-ui">Edit the front plate out</b> (on a front photo: the bumper is filled in, no box), or choose <b class="gd-ui">A CarmaCars plate</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Pixelation</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Blur</b>. Photos covered the old way are made again the new way by themselves.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the covered photo</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Clear the boxes</b> starts over.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">No plate in the shot? Press <b class="gd-ui">No plate visible on this photo</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:690/703"><img src="/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-desktop-4219ad93.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="690" height="703"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:42.5%;top:83.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:49.6%;top:29.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:4.3%;top:77.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:15.5%;top:83.8%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18.1%;top:91.2%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately. Keyboard: N adds a box, the arrows move it, Shift and the arrows resize it, Delete removes it.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-publish" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A real car that is not on the site is a line on To do: press <b class="gd-ui">Set rates and publish</b>. The daily rate is filled in (the car&#39;s own, or the suggested rate from similar cars or the class); change it if you like and press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On the car itself, the Listing tab has <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>; each open item of its checklist has a button to where it is done.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">From a listing review: press <b class="gd-ui">Approve and publish</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Approve, publish later</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Send back</b> with what to fix.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>The plate check never holds a car back: a real photo whose plate is not checked stays private (the other photos, or the sample photos, show instead) and goes public by itself once its plate is covered or marked not visible. Listings already live show &quot;Plate not checked&quot; on such photos.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-photos-filed-under-the-wrong-shot-and-interior-windows" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Photos filed under the wrong shot, and interior windows</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the Photos card, each shot lists its photos. A photo filed under the wrong shot: press <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> under it, then <b class="gd-ui">Remove it</b>. The shot is free again: take or pick the right photo. The removed photo is kept privately and the removal is in the history. A live listing&#39;s photos change in the review instead (Reject).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Dashboard and seat photos: what shows through the windows is replaced by the studio background when the cut is clean (a quality check: some but not most of the frame seen through, high in the frame, a few clean regions, sharp edges). Otherwise the windows are blurred, and the photo is marked windows blurred. Nothing to do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-listing-without-photos-yet-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A listing without photos yet: sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p">A car can be listed before its photos are taken. Until then the site shows a sample photo.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Submit the listing without photos. The listing copy is still written for you from the car&#39;s details.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The car page and the car&#39;s card show a sample photo, captioned &quot;Sample photo&quot;, so renters know it is not this car. Staff see &quot;Using sample photos&quot; on the car and in Listings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Publishing does not wait for a plate check: a sample photo has no plate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add the real photos when they are taken. Once real photos are approved they replace the sample at once; nothing else to do.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sample photos</b>. The pictures a car shows until its real photos are in.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every body type has a built-in picture (sedan, SUV, truck, van, coupe, hatchback, electric car).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Add your own: choose the Body type, and a Make and Model if the photo is of that exact model, pick the Photo, and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the photo</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The most specific photo wins: make and model, then make and body type, then body type. <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Delete</b> a photo you no longer want.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Cars using sample photos lists the cars still waiting for real photos. Each real car showing sample photos is also a line on To do, with <b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings/sample-photos</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/812"><img src="/guides/img/admin-36-sample-photos-desktop-55c64070.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="812"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:26.8%;top:28.9%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-publish-now-and-new-cars-published-by-themselves" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish now, and new cars published by themselves</h2><p class="gd-p">Nothing between a new car and the site has to be finished first: the car goes on the site, and what is still open shows on its checklist.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Publish new cars automatically</b> (on by default): a new real car goes on the site by itself as soon as it has its year, make and model and its rates, when it is added with rates, when its rates are saved, when it is added for an owner, or when an owner&#39;s application is approved.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Otherwise open the car: its Listing tab says why it is not on the site and has <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>. A car with no rates yet is published with the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults in Program settings); change them later on the Rates tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Every real car has its listing from the moment it is added, as a draft. It shows in Listings and in Not on the site yet until it is published.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An owner&#39;s own application waits for your decision before its car is published by itself; Publish now still works.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A car taken off the site by staff, or scheduled for a later date, is never published by itself: press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-checklist-what-is-still-open-on-a-listed-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The checklist: what is still open on a listed car</h2><p class="gd-p">Open items never stop publishing. They show as warnings on the car&#39;s Listing tab and after Publish now.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Paperwork</td><td>Ownership permit, registry forms, agreements signed, Forms C and D, upfront payment, registry visit, tracker, safety certificate</td></tr><tr><td>Insurance</td><td>Not on the fleet insurance policy yet: the car can be booked, but not handed over</td></tr><tr><td>Details</td><td>Colour, body, seats, gearbox: the car page leaves out what is missing</td></tr><tr><td>Photos</td><td>No real photos: sample photos stand in. A photo whose plate is not checked stays private until it is</td></tr><tr><td>No VIN yet</td><td>A car added by its plate alone: add the VIN when you have it</td></tr><tr><td>Possible duplicate</td><td>An open flag in Similar cars. Only Same car keeps the car off the site</td></tr><tr><td>Owner terms</td><td>The management fee (Revenue Share) and fees not set: a request uses the owner&#39;s terms or the standard grid</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-fleet-policy-rule-at-handover" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The fleet policy rule at handover</h2><p class="gd-p">A program owner&#39;s car is listed and can be requested, offered and paid for while its paperwork is open. It is never handed over until the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet insurance policy.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Staff see a warning on a request and an offer for a car not on the policy yet.</li><li>The handover refuses the car until the insurer&#39;s confirmation is recorded (Owners and onboarding). The field app says so on the job.</li><li>Only real states keep a car off the site: retired, left the program, out of service, Turo only, bookings turned off, a self-managed owner in arrears, or a paused listing.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-cars-on-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cars on sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> ends with <b class="gd-ui">Cars on sample photos</b>: each real car whose page still shows sample photos, with its newest handover photos (the check-in and check-out photos field staff take).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Where a handover photographed the car, press <b class="gd-ui">Use the handover photos</b>. They go into the car&#39;s listing as if taken on the capture screen.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When every required shot is there, the listing is submitted: the studio editor puts the car on the CarmaCars backdrop, then the listing waits for your review like any other.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with no handover photos yet gets them at its next handover, or press <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> and take them.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The studio editor uses Cloudflare image transformations (5,000 a month included). Settings &gt; Usage counts them.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-car-s-registration-and-documents" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car&#39;s registration and documents</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, then <b class="gd-ui">Owner &amp; documents</b>. The <b class="gd-ui">Registration</b> card:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Correct the <b class="gd-ui">VIN</b> (it is checked: 17 characters, the check digit, not on another car; decoded again for the body style and trim), the <b class="gd-ui">Year</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Body style</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Type the <b class="gd-ui">Ontario permit number</b> and the date the <b class="gd-ui">Plate sticker expires</b>. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before; save the new date after the renewal and the task closes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>, choose the kind (<b class="gd-ui">Ownership permit</b>, Safety Standards Certificate, owner&#39;s insurance, other), pick the photo or PDF and press <b class="gd-ui">Upload</b>. The ownership permit clears that item of the owner&#39;s checklist.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">For the <b class="gd-ui">Safety Standards Certificate</b>, also type its number, the date it was issued and the date it expires. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before it expires; upload the new certificate with its dates and the task closes. It is a document on the car, not a service record, and nothing is billed to the owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b> takes the ownership permit and the Safety Standards Certificate too, under <b class="gd-ui">Documents (optional)</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-car-added-under-the-wrong-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car added under the wrong owner</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, Overview, <b class="gd-ui">Who supplies the car</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Move to another owner</b>. Choose the owner, or <b class="gd-ui">CarmaCars (owner not known yet)</b>: the car becomes a company car, with no owner schedule or terms.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The car&#39;s unsigned owner application and vehicle schedule are withdrawn (kept in the history), and its draft owner invoices are deleted. Nobody is notified.</li><li>It is refused once anything for the car is signed, issued, paid or on a statement.</li></ul><h3 class="gd-h3">The VIN from the car, not typed</h3><p class="gd-p">Every VIN field (Add a car, Add a car for an owner, the car&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Registration</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b>) has <b class="gd-ui">Scan the barcode</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Photo of the VIN</b>. Scan the barcode in the driver&#39;s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield: the phone&#39;s camera reads it by itself. Or take a photo of the VIN plate or sticker: the barcode in it is read first, else the photo is read for the printed VIN. The VIN is checked (17 characters, the check digit; I, O and Q become 1 and 0) and decoded as when you type it. Check it against the car before saving.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Photos in any order</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> on the listing takes any number of photos at once from the camera roll. Each is sorted to its shot by itself (front three-quarter, sides, rear, dashboard, seats and the rest); a shot that already has its photo sends the new one to the extra photos, so nothing is replaced by accident. The shots are a guide, not a rule: a listing is complete with 10 photos that can go on the site and one outside photo for the cover. Outside photos get the studio background: the car is cropped to its edges and placed big in the frame with its wheels on the floor and a soft shadow under the tyres, and any corner watermark or caption beside the car is left out. Inside and detail photos are kept as taken; when one has a watermark, a logo or caption text on it, the edge with the mark is cut off by itself, and a photo whose mark cannot be cut off (one in the middle) stays off the site until you replace it. <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b> opens on every outside photo with the plate box suggested; check it and save.</p><p class="gd-p">Outside photos made before the newest framing (the car small in the frame, or without the model&#39;s name behind it) are made again with <b class="gd-ui">Frame the outside photos again</b> above the photos of the listing, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, frame again</b>. The cover and the main outside views get the model&#39;s name lettered behind the car, as on the sample photos (for example CLA, C CLASS, AMG GT). The photos leave the site until their plates are checked again: the plate box is suggested on the new photos; check each and cover it. On a published listing each goes back on the site once its plate is checked.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-showroom-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Showroom photos</h2><p class="gd-p">Outside photos go in the dark CarmaCars showroom by themselves: a simple dark dealership with linear lights in the ceiling, a slatted wood wall between two light strips with a big lit CarmaCars sign, and a polished dark floor with the car&#39;s reflection and a shadow under each tyre. Every angle of a car is in the same room, and the cover has the model&#39;s name in metal letters on the wall under the sign. The image model may relight the car or turn it slightly; a photo that shows another car, model or colour is not used. <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> has the switch (Showroom photos, on), the image model that makes the photos look photographed, and its daily limit. Past the limit, or when the image model is not available, the site makes the showroom itself for free, and the photo says why under it.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A car whose photos were made on the black studio: press <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to this car</b> above its photos, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, apply</b>.</li><li>Every car at once: <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Showroom photos</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to every car</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, every car</b>.</li><li>Under a photo in the showroom: <b class="gd-ui">Redo</b> makes it again, <b class="gd-ui">Back to the original</b> puts back the version before the showroom.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">A car that stays where it was keeps its plate check. When the image model made the photo, check the plate again: the photo is off the site until you do. Photos made in the first showroom are made again in the new one with <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to this car</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to every car</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-failed-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Failed photos</h2><p class="gd-p">The site makes the photo sizes itself: the image service is asked only to cut the car out (<b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>: the switch to let the image service make every photo step is off). When the image service is busy or over its allowance, the photo still goes on the site from the original and is made again later. A listing marked Failed has <b class="gd-ui">Retry failed photos</b> in its note; <b class="gd-ui">Retry failed photos</b> at the top does every listing. They are made again a few at a time, and the listing leaves Failed when they are done.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-first-photo-plain-with-a-model-or-a-flyer" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The first photo: plain, with a model, or a flyer</h2><p class="gd-p">On a listing, under <b class="gd-ui">First photo</b>, choose what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit. Switch any time; the other photos stay as they are.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Plain car</b>: the cover photo as it is (the default).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">With a model</b>: a car-show photo made by the image model, with a fully clothed adult model beside the car. It needs the image model; until it is made (or when the image model is not there) the plain cover shows, and the listing says why.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Flyer</b>: the cover photo with a band like a printed flyer: the car, the price a day from its live rates, the call to action, a badge and the logo. When the price, the words or the cover photo change, it is made again by itself within 10 minutes; the plain cover shows meanwhile.</li></ul><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Make it again</b> makes the chosen one again. The words of the flyer and the description of the model are in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> (First photo &quot;flyer&quot; and First photo &quot;with a model&quot;); {car}, {price}, {weekly} and {monthly} are filled for each car.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-marketing-photos-in-other-scenes" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Marketing photos in other scenes</h2><p class="gd-p">For Marketplace and social posts, a car&#39;s outside photos can be made again in other scenes. The website keeps its own photos in the dark showroom: a marketing set never replaces them.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a listing, under <b class="gd-ui">Marketing photos</b>, choose a scene, or <b class="gd-ui">Mix: a different scene on each photo</b>, and press <b class="gd-ui">Make the marketing set</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The copies show as they are made. The dark showroom and the plain white studio are made by the site when the image model is not there; the photographic scenes (a bright showroom, a city street at night, the Toronto waterfront, a parking garage, Highway, a scenic road, Brick building) need the image model, and say so on the copy when it is not there.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Download (ZIP)</b> takes the set; the Marketplace kit&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">With scenes (ZIP)</b> takes the same set.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Marketing scenes</b> lists the scenes. A scene made in a real place has a photo of that place: Brick building picks its photo by itself: the widest outside photo, as taken, of the shareholders&#39; own cars. To use another, press <b class="gd-ui">Change the reference photo</b> and pick one (the shareholders&#39; cars&#39; photos come first), or upload one. The scenes&#39; names and words are in the <b class="gd-ui">Marketing scenes</b> setting.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-extra-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Extra photos</h2><p class="gd-p">A photo that fits no shot is an extra photo. Under the shots, <b class="gd-ui">Extra outside photos</b> (put on the studio background) and <b class="gd-ui">Extra inside and detail photos</b> (touched up) each take any number at once. They count toward the 10 photos, get the same plate check, and come after the standard shots on the car&#39;s page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">In the review, <b class="gd-ui">Extra photos, in their order on the car page</b> lists them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Drag a photo by its handle (⋮⋮), or press <b class="gd-ui">Earlier</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Later</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the order</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-fix-a-cut-out" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fix a cut-out</h2><p class="gd-p">When the background removal cuts badly (a mirror or a wheel missing, background left beside the car), press <b class="gd-ui">Edit the cut-out</b> under the outside photo.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Cut-out</b> shows the car over the photo as taken, shown faintly. Choose <b class="gd-ui">Erase</b> and brush over what should go, or <b class="gd-ui">Restore</b> and brush over what the cut-out took off. Set <b class="gd-ui">Brush size</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Zoom</b>; when zoomed, <b class="gd-ui">Move the view</b> pans. <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> takes back the last stroke.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">On the studio</b> shows the car on the studio background. Drag the car to move it and use <b class="gd-ui">Size</b> to make it larger or smaller. <b class="gd-ui">Centre and full size</b> puts it back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save as a new version</b>. The photo is made again in about a minute; the version before and the photo as taken are kept. <b class="gd-ui">Reset to the automatic cut-out</b> starts again from the automatic one.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>If the car did not move, the plate check carries over: a photo marked no plate visible stays so, and a covered plate is covered again on the new photo when the review is open. If the car moved, check the plate again. A photo made before cut-outs were kept shows <b class="gd-ui">Make the cut-out</b> first; the editor opens by itself when it is ready.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">Every photo also gets a light touch-up by itself (exposure, levels, a little contrast and colour, mild sharpening), never enough to change the paint colour or hide a scratch. Turn it off for one photo with <b class="gd-ui">Use original colours</b> under it (the photo is made again; approve it again), or for every photo in Admin &gt; Settings &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> (Listings) with <b class="gd-ui">Auto-enhance listing photos</b>. The photo as uploaded is always kept.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-import-photos-from-a-google-drive-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Import photos from a Google Drive link</h2><p class="gd-p">The owner often hands over a car&#39;s photos as a public Google Drive folder, or one big folder with a folder per make and then per car. You do not download them: paste the link.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">One car.</b> On the car&#39;s listing, under the capture, <b class="gd-ui">Import photos from a Google Drive link</b>. Paste the folder link (shared with Anyone with the link) and press <b class="gd-ui">Import the photos</b>. Every photo in the folder, and in the folders inside it, is added to this car as if you had pressed Add photos: each is sorted to its shot (else filed as an extra photo, in file-name order), put on the studio background and checked for its plate. The box under the link, <b class="gd-ui">Submit the listing for processing when its photos are in</b>, is on by default.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Many cars.</b> <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Import photos from Drive</b> (a button on Vehicles). Paste the top folder&#39;s link and press <b class="gd-ui">Read the folder</b>. The page walks every folder and proposes a car for each folder that holds photos, from the year, make, model, colour and plate in the folder names (the make folder above counts; 01 Motors partner cars come first). Check the table: tick or untick <b class="gd-ui">Import</b>, change the car in the list (the likely cars come first), leave out a folder with <b class="gd-ui">Do not import this folder</b>. A line marked <b class="gd-ui">Check this one</b> matched two alike cars. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Import N photos from M folders</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The page follows the import by itself. You can leave it and come back: it runs in the background.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The end shows the summary: imported, skipped and failed, and why for each (a file over 15 MB, a file that is not a photo, the same photo already on the car, a folder not shared).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Try the failed photos again</b> takes only the ones that failed. Pressing Import on the same link again never adds a photo twice: a Drive file already on the car is skipped, and so is the same picture under another name. A photo you took off the car can be imported again.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>JPG, PNG, HEIC and WebP only (HEIC and WebP are made JPEG first). At most 15 MB a photo, 600 photos, 400 folders and 4 GB in one import. Drive is asked politely, one photo at a time; a big import takes a while.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Without a key, Drive shows only the first 50 files of a folder on its public page; a folder with more is read in full when Drive allows it. In <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Photo import from Google Drive</b> box takes a Google API key with the Drive API on (after it is saved only its last 4 characters are shown, and it is never written to the change log): with it, folders of any size are read and photos download without Drive&#39;s warning pages.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-pickup-from-owner-and-return-to-owner-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pickup from owner and return to owner (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Pickup from owner and return to owner</b> records the car&#39;s condition when CarmaCars picks it up from its owner or gives it back: the date and time, km, fuel, many photos at once with the suggested angles, and notes. <b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> adds more to a record later. The owner sees these records read only on the car&#39;s page in their portal. They are the baseline condition for any dispute.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-incident-cards-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Incident cards (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Incident cards</b> prints the card for each car: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, the support number from Settings, a roadside number when there is one, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. Open a car and press <b class="gd-ui">Incident card</b> to print only that car; on the list, <b class="gd-ui">Print all cars</b> prints them all, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks, ready to laminate. Under Fleet insurance policy press <b class="gd-ui">Add the policy</b> (the insurer, the policy number, the dates, the named insured, the roadside number on the slip) and choose the uploaded slip if you have one: it is printed as it is, otherwise the fields are. The card never shows a premium. Fleet staff print the same cards from their portal.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-field-jobs-shifts-and-who-gets-a-job" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Field jobs, shifts and who gets a job</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Field jobs</b>, is the board Fleet uses, with every action Fleet has. Field staff take shifts you publish with <b class="gd-ui">Publish shifts</b>. Jobs go on shifts, not on people: each job is put on the shift covering its time (or that day&#39;s), whoever holds the shift does it (several people share the jobs, least busy first), a shift nobody holds keeps its jobs for whoever claims it, and work lands only on days with shifts (work due on a day without shifts moves to the day before, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day; the booking&#39;s own times never change). A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning on the board and on the booking. <b class="gd-ui">To a shift</b> moves a job to another shift. You can give a job to a field person on a shift that day or to an Admin, take it off with <b class="gd-ui">Unassign</b> (tick <b class="gd-ui">Tell them</b> to let them know), and an Admin who holds a job opens it on the field portal. A person who has not passed the academy cannot be given a job or take a shift. A shift with jobs and nobody on it within 24 hours alerts Fleet and the Admins once.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'settings', 'chapter', 'search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides', 'Settings change the public site and the rules of the program at once. Program settings are kept as dated rows, so earlier values stay on record.

## The Settings page

1. Site setup lists what is still missing on the public site, with **Open site settings**.
2. Site settings: contact details, hours, tagline, logo, socials, Google place id and featured cars.
3. Program settings: every timing and policy value.
4. Forms: Blind Spot''s rental agreement for every booking, and the official ServiceOntario PDFs and what goes in each field.
5. Insurers: insurance companies billed for bookings.

![](/guides/img/admin-24-settings-desktop-89b31691.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 900; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings; pins: 1 32.6 33.0, 2 25.8 40.2, 3 77.4 40.2, 4 25.8 73.2, 5 25.8 84.9")

The other tiles: Site content (headings, FAQs, legal text), Fee defaults, Deposit tiers, Kilometre choices, Vehicle classes, Vehicle class rules, Airports and delivery, Protection Plan prices, Card coverage, Reviews, Quo contacts (everyone with a phone number as a contact in Quo: see Texts and calls), Text alerts, Partners (each partner company''s CRM link: see Partners, company cars and rentals added by hand), Email aliases and reply-to, My profile, Staff and roles, Promo codes and Quick replies.

**My profile**: the greeting name of this login. To do greets it whole ("Good morning, Abbas and Mahad" on a login the owners share) and the assistant uses it; empty, the first name of the account. Press **Change the greeting name**, type it and save.

## Program settings

1. Buffer between trips (90 minutes): the time held before and after every trip, in every availability and conflict check (requests, offers, date changes, extensions, the calendar). The cleaning block after a trip is this time; Turnaround between trips is the same number. A booking already closer than this is not changed: the calendar rings it.
1. Late fee and extensions (Booking requests and offers): the late fee per started hour (17.5% of the daily rate, at least $25; new bookings and offers only), the extension discounts (5% for a day or more, 10% for 1 or 3 hours) and **Approve a renter''s extension at once when nothing needs a person** (on). A car''s own switch is in Fleet, the car, **Edit details**: **Renters extend themselves**.
2. Settings come in groups such as Company, Booking requests and offers, Owner debits and statement emails, Deposits, Delivery, Owners and fleet, and Tolls and damage. Open one to see its fields.
3. First reply target for customer service and sales (minutes), under Booking requests and offers: 5 by default. New booking requests, enquiries, changes renters ask for and renter messages are due that many minutes after they come in; the scorecard and the staff screens use it. What renters are told (Reply wording, in Site settings) is separate.
4. Staff commissions and prices typed by hand: the commission outside Sales (10%), the three Sales tiers and their days (10%, 15% from 50 days, 20% from 100 days, the month''s target), the price floor a day (empty: none) and the discount from the rate sheet that flags a price (20%). The owner confirmed these values in October 2026. The remote Sales values follow: the three remote tiers (5%, 10%, 15%), the touches a month (400), the drop under it (one tier) and its floor (2.5%), the peak hours a week (20), the reply target (15 minutes) and the peak hours (noon to 6 pm, Thursday to Sunday).
5. Staff agreement defaults by function, at the bottom: pay (a month, an hour or commission only), the rate, the schedule (full time, part time or flexible), days a week and hours a day for Customer service, Fleet, Finance and Sales, the values every assistant shares, and the field staff wage. Sales is commission only: no rate and a flexible schedule. Press **Save the defaults**.
6. Live visitors and live chat: recording visits, the signal thresholds, follow-up tasks, the chat and its assistant, and how long visits and chats are kept.
7. Discount games: the same values as Settings, Discount games (the prize table and the games are easier to change there).
8. Deposits: the toll and ticket window after the return (7 days: settling sooner suggests a hold-back), the longest hold-back (30 days after the return), how long before a card hold lapses it is collected (36 hours), and collecting what is owed after the deposit by itself (the card on file, then a pay link, then a Finance task). A deposit is never released by itself.
9. Field jobs and handovers: field jobs made from each confirmed booking (on) and who gets them (the least busy field staff member, or nobody so Fleet assigns), how field staff may take a deposit at the check-in besides a card (e-Transfer and cash), and whether they may release a car whose tracker is not reporting, with a reason (on; you get an urgent task). Field pay: the first day of a pay period (every period is two weeks), the default hourly rate (CA$18.00), whether overtime is paid (off), after how many hours in a week (44) and at what share of the rate (150%), vacation pay added to each statement (off; Ontario 4%) and the longest shift (16 hours).
10. Sign-in by phone: codes by text from the CarmaCars number (on), US numbers (off until the Quo number is registered for US texting, A2P 10DLC), codes per number and per connection an hour, and whether a verified phone confirms an account like a confirmed email. Accepting an offer, signing and paying need a confirmed account; an account made by phone gives its email on the pay page before its first payment.
11. Calendar sync, Turo by email, Booking recovery emails and Site check: how often calendar links are read, the Turo inbound address and who may forward to it, the reminder delays and sending hours, and the site check with the address its alerts go to (rent@carmacars.ca), the minutes before an email, the daily limit and the quiet hours.
12. Change a value and press **Save**. It is saved as a new row from today; the rows before stay as they were.

![](/guides/img/admin-25-program-settings-desktop-d16b066c.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1000; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings/program; pins: 1 25.8 22.0, 2 27.8 49.0")


## Lead-time pricing

A car booked at short notice costs a little more and one booked well ahead a little less. Open **Settings**, then **Program settings**: Lead-time pricing is at the top.

1. The switch turns it on or off for every car (on by default).
2. The table holds the tiers: when the pickup is that many hours away, the rental charge changes by that percentage. By default: under 24 hours +15%, 24 to 72 hours +10%, 3 to 13 days 0%, 14 days or more −5%. Type the hours and the percentage on each row (a minus for less); **Add a tier** adds one, **Remove** takes one off. Each row shows what it does to a $500 rental.
3. **Also adjust bookings billed to an insurer** is off by default: an insurer pays its own rate, never a short-notice premium.
4. Press **Save lead-time pricing**. New quotes and requests use it; bookings already made keep theirs.

| What it touches | How |
| --- | --- |
| The rental charge | The percentage of the rental charge only, before tax: one line in the price, "Short-notice pricing +10%" or "Booked ahead −5%". Never the fees, the deposit or add-ons |
| When it is worked out | When the quote is made (the car page, the cars list once dates are chosen, the request), from that moment to the pickup on Toronto clocks. "From $X a day" stays at the base rate |
| When it is locked | On the request: the offer, a change of dates and the payment keep the same percentage |
| Other discounts | The non-refundable discount, a promo code and a staff discount are worked out on the rental charge from the rates, as before, and show beside it |
| Owner revenue and commissions | Count the rental charge after it, as they count the discounts |
| Staff | Change it on a booking under **More options** on the review screen; a price typed by hand replaces it. Rentals added by hand, Owner Bookings and placeholders are not adjusted |

> Tip: A car can turn it off or have its own tiers: **Vehicles** > the car > **Rates** > Lead-time pricing for this car.
## Vehicle class rules

Open **Settings**, then **Vehicle class rules**. How a new car''s class is decided from its VIN: the first rule that matches wins.

1. The table lists each rule: its rank, what the car must be (a make, and patterns for the model, the trim and the body), the class it gets, the class once the car is old enough, a note and whether it is on. The lowest rank that matches is used; a car that matches no rule is Standard.
2. Press **Add a rule** or **Change**: a rank, at least one condition, the class, optionally the years old after which an older class applies, and a note (it is shown as the reason for the class). A pattern is not case sensitive: ^911 matches models that start with 911. A rule with no condition, a pattern that does not compile and an older class equal to the class are refused.
3. **Try a car** gives the class the rules decide for a year, make, model, trim and body, and why.
4. **Delete** removes a rule; switch it off instead to keep it. Every add, change and delete is in the audit log, with before and after.

> Tip: A rule changes the cars entered from then on. A car already listed keeps its class until you change it on the car.

## Official ServiceOntario forms

The five official forms are loaded with a mapping to the owner, car, company and lender details. Each is the form exactly as ServiceOntario publishes it: only its empty text boxes are filled; its own text and layout are never changed. A form whose stored PDF is not the publisher''s download (or your upload of it) gives owners the data sheet instead. Its checkboxes, drop-downs and signatures are done by hand at the counter, in ink. Until you check a form, owners get a data sheet with the values.

1. Open **Settings** > **Forms**. Each form shows "Mapping to check" (a draft is ready) or "Official PDF in use". Its notes say what the form is for and which boxes are left blank on purpose.
2. Choose **Preview with**: a sample car (made-up values) or one of the cars. Press **Download a filled preview** and check each value against the form. The preview uses the mapping on screen, saved or not.
3. Change a field if needed: What goes in it (or "Signed here by hand, in ink"), a Format (for example YYYY/MM/DD) and Only when. Write what you changed and press Save the mapping. **Earlier mappings** lists every save, with who and when; **Load** puts one back on screen to preview and save again. Fleet can map the forms too (Owners > Government forms), but only an Admin uploads a form.
4. Press **Checked: use for owners**. Every owner''s form of that kind is filled again, except ones already signed or filed. Owners download it, print it and sign it in ink; record it with **Record an official form signed in ink**. Each form not checked yet is also a line on To do with the same button and Preview it.
5. A new version from ServiceOntario? Press **Upload the official fillable PDF**: the fields of the same name keep their mapping.

> Good to know: SR-LV-006 (registration), SR-LV-012 (two registrants), ON00453 (a company''s RIN), 013-1155 and 013-0169 (the tax-exempt transfer into an owner''s corporation). 013-1155 is sworn before a commissioner, so it is printed and signed in person. ON00453 is an Adobe form: it opens in Adobe Acrobat Reader. Each form''s notes list what to tick or choose at the counter. A car gets only the forms its onboarding method needs: no form for a Transfer of a car owned outright or financed (the sign-back on the permit), 013-1155 and 013-0169 only for a Lease through a new Owner Corporation.

## Blind Spot rental agreement

We rent under Blind Spot Car Rental''s insurance, so every booking has two agreements: CarmaCars'' rental agreement and Blind Spot''s own. Blind Spot''s is filled in from the booking, the renter and the car, and the renter signs both with one signature. Its PDF is stored privately, never on the website.

1. Open **Settings** > **Forms**. The Blind Spot Car Rental agreement card is first. Press **Upload Blind Spot''s PDF** and choose Blind Spot''s blank form (2 pages, A4).
2. Press **Download the filled sample**: a made-up booking on the form. **Sample billed to an insurer** also fills the claim number, the adjuster and the insurance company. Check every box.
3. On the form the old address (top left and twice in box 15) is replaced by the mailing address of Site settings, box 1 by CarmaCars'' HST number (Program settings, Company HST number; blank until it is entered), and box 21 has the representative''s signature instead of Sam''s.
4. Press **Checked: use for bookings**. From then on each booking gets it when its rental agreement is made; a renter whose agreement is already open gets it the next time they open the signing page.
5. Box 21: Ahmad is written in a script hand, as Blind Spot asked. To use a real signature instead, upload a PNG under Authorized company representative; Remove the image goes back to the written name. Full name is for the signature record page.
6. A new version of Blind Spot''s form? Upload it the same way: it waits for **Checked: use for bookings**, and bookings keep the version in use until then.

> Good to know: Each box is filled only when the booking has the value: the renter and their licence, the additional drivers, the car (plate, make and model, the fleet number as vehicle number), the pickup as time and date out, the due-back date and time, the kilometres allowed, the rate rows (days, weeks or months @ the rate = the amount; a rental counted by the day, such as 31 days at the monthly rate, shows its daily rate rounded to the cent, and box 14 says how the charge was made), the underage fee, the Protection Plan as CDW, winter tires, the subtotal, HST (13% of the subtotal), total and deposit, the deposit received and the day it was taken (before pickup, the amount due at pickup), and for a booking billed to an insurer the insurer, claim number and adjuster. Other charges, such as delivery, are listed in box 14. The boxes filled at check-in and check-out stay blank until then. The fuel gauges are covered and the level of the check-in report (fuel out) and the check-out report (fuel in) is written in words, blank with no reading.

The renter''s signature goes in boxes 16, 17 and 20 of the signed copy, with the day they signed beside box 20 and a signature record page. Each later version (as picked up, as returned, corrected) carries the same signature and day. Both agreements are in the booking''s Drivers and documents tab, in the renter''s Documents, and the signed Blind Spot agreement is attached to the "Your signed rental agreement" email. Admin > Today lists the HST number, the upload and the check until they are done.

## Agreements to sign: investors and staff

Investment agreements and staff agreements are made from the person''s record and signed in their own portal, with the e-signature (never on paper).

1. Investor: open **People** > **Investors** and the investor. Under Investment agreement, press **Send the agreement to sign**. Check the values it is filled with (amount, yearly percentage, dates, exemption) and press **Send to sign**.
2. Once the investor signs, the agreement shows **Awaiting countersignature** on the investor''s page and on To do. It is not countersigned automatically: check it and press **Countersign**. CarmaCars is bound once it has countersigned and the funds clear.
3. Staff: open **People** > **Team**. Under Staff agreements, press **Send the agreement to sign** beside the person. Pay, schedule, hours and the other values start from the staff profile and the defaults of their function in Program settings; change any before sending. For Sales the Pay is Commission only: the agreement then has no rate, schedule or hours, and pays the commission of section 3.4.
4. A field staff member''s agreement prints the home address they entered themselves. Staff enter their home address at their first sign-in, before they sign, or in their profile.
5. They get a notice, check the key values and sign in their portal in a few taps (their name is the signature, or they draw it). The signed copy is filed with their documents.
6. Your own PDF instead? **Send a PDF to sign** still works.
7. Sent by mistake? Press **Withdraw** and give the reason.

## The user guides

**Settings** > **Guides**. The guide of each portal, as people read it under Guide.

1. Each guide shows its version, when it was published and whether there are unpublished changes.
2. Open a guide and press a section. Change its text and press **Show the preview** to see it as people will. Press **Save the draft**; each save is kept in the section''s history.
3. Move a section with the arrows, hide it, or press **Add a chapter**. Upload a screenshot under Screenshots and paste the line it gives you.
4. Press **Publish version** (the next number). The portals show the new version at once.
5. The stored PDF is printed again by the guides-pdf workflow. Until then the guide says the web guide has newer edits.

## The guides keep up by themselves

After every update of the site that changes the portals, the guides are checked without anyone asking.

1. Every screenshot is taken again on the new version of the site. One whose screen changed replaces the old one in the guide.
2. The text of each section whose screen changed, or that names a button the portals no longer show, is rewritten from the portal''s own labels and menu, checked, and published. The PDFs of those guides are printed again.
3. Such a section says **Changed automatically on** and the date, in the list of guides and in the guide''s editor. Not right? Open the section and press **Revert**: the text it replaced comes back, published at once.
4. This includes sections you edited: the newest automatic text is published, and every earlier version stays in the section''s history. There is nothing to review.
5. A rewrite that does not pass the checks is asked again, more strictly. If it still does not pass, the screenshots and button names are updated, the rest of the text stays as it was, and the next run tries again.

> Tip: The card "The guides keep up by themselves" at the top of Guides lists the last runs: when, how many screenshots were replaced, how many sections were rewritten, and how many PDFs were printed.

## Insurers and the other lists

1. Open Insurers. Each insurer on file opens to edit its billing contact, email, phone, address and notes. Its rates by car class are in **Money** > **Insurers**.
2. To add one, fill in the Add form (Name, Billing contact, Billing email and the rest) and press **Add**.
3. Deposit tiers, Kilometre choices, Vehicle classes, Airports, Promo codes and Quick replies work the same way.

## Promo codes: end dates and reminders

**Settings**, **Promo codes**.

- Every code made for a person has an end date: a game prize 7 days, a come-back offer 30, a Live visitors code 3 and a code made for one renter 30 unless you set another. The first card of Promo codes holds the 30 days and the two reminders.
- A code for everyone may have no end date: empty Valid until. The Add form starts with an end date 30 days ahead.
- A code that ended is refused wherever it is typed (the request form, an offer, Add a rental, a booking edit) with "This code has expired".
- A person who has not used a code is reminded 3 days before its last day and the day before, by email and by text as they chose, never once they used it, unsubscribed or the code ended, and never twice. A game code reminder always goes; a reminder of any other code needs their consent to offers.
- The list shows each code''s end date and the reminders sent. The card Codes sent to people lists game prizes, come-back offers and Live visitors codes the same way.

## Card coverage: which credit cards include rental car coverage

**Settings** > **Card coverage** is the list renters see at `carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage` and staff see under Card coverage in their portal. It starts filled in with 48 Canadian and US cards, each checked on October 23, 2026.

1. The table shows each card: who pays first (Primary, Secondary, or not stated), the car value limit (MSRP), the longest rental, whether the numbers were read in the issuer''s own document, and when it was last checked.
2. Open a card under Change a card, open its official guide, correct what changed and press **Save**. Changing the facts without a date marks the card checked today; type a Last checked date to record another day.
3. A card whose numbers come from a published summary has Read in the issuer''s own document unticked and the summary''s link under Where the numbers came from. The page shows it as Unverified. Tick it once you have read the issuer''s guide.
4. Add a card with the Add form; untick Shown to hide one. Changes reach the public page at once.

> Tip: A card not checked for 6 months shows on Today until it is checked again. The page tells renters to confirm with their card issuer and says CarmaCars decides no claims: keep the list to facts from the issuer''s guide.

## Reviews: review requests and Google

**Settings** > **Reviews**: when review requests go, the Google review link and the Google Business Profile connection. Review requests are on from the start.

1. When review requests go: the check-out (on or off, the shortest rental, hours after the pickup), the request (minutes after the check-out), the reminder (hours) and the final follow-up (days), the sending hours (9 am to 9 pm), and the hold while charges are open.
2. The Google review link: the Google place id (Site settings) makes it, or paste the Business Profile''s own review link.
3. Google Business Profile: press **Connect Google** and sign in with rent@carmacars.ca, then allow access. Reviews are read every 6 hours and matched to renters by name within 30 days after their return.
4. A clear match stops that renter''s reminders at once. A possible match waits in Reviews: press **Confirm**, **Not this renter** or **Match to a booking**.

> Tip: Until Google approves the Business Profile API for the project, the status says so and nothing else changes: renters still get the review link, and "I already left a review", Mark reviewed and on-site reviews still stop the messages.

### Pair the card reader
**Settings** > **Card reader**. On the Stripe S700, swipe from the left edge, open **Settings**, then **Generate pairing code**. Type the three words in **Pairing code**, name the reader (Front desk) and press **Pair reader**. The first time, a Stripe Terminal location is made from the mailing address in Site settings: write it as street, city, province and postal code. **Remove** takes a reader off the list. Card statements read 18122211 Canada Inc., the Stripe account''s statement descriptor.

### Rewards
**Settings** > **Rewards**. CarmaCars Rewards is on: 1 point per dollar of the rental charge after discounts (never fees, add-ons, coverage, tax or the deposit), 100 points = $1, redeemed from 500 points as a code of the renter''s own, valid 90 days. Points end 12 months after the last rental or redemption, with a reminder email 30 days before.

1. **Ways to earn**: each on or off with its points. Referral (500 to the referrer, 250 to the friend, at the friend''s first completed rental), a follow on Instagram, TikTok or Facebook (50 each, once, granted on the click from the Rewards page, since a follow cannot be checked; a platform shows only with its page in Site settings), a review on carmacars.ca (100, any rating; the review shows "Received reward points"), a Google review (100 a rental, any rating, on the renter''s word: they press I posted my review and give the name on it; hidden until the Google review page is set here), a damage-free rental (200: no damage, claim, cleaning or smoking fee, back on time), the birthday (100) and the first rental (100).
2. **Tiers**: Member, Silver from 10 rental days in 12 months (5% off) and Gold from 30 (10% off), with a perk staff honour on request. The discount is a promo code of the renter''s own.
3. Points, tier discounts and codes come off the rental charge only and reduce Owner Revenue like any promo code.
4. **Google reviews claimed** lists every claim; **Reverse** takes the points back with a reason. **A renter''s points**: find the renter, then **Add or take off points** with a reason, or reverse any entry (for example, referral fraud).

### Setup checklist
**Settings** shows what still needs a key from one of CarmaCars'' own accounts. **Add to Apple Wallet** stays hidden until the Apple Pass Type ID certificate is added (WALLET_PASS_CERT, WALLET_PASS_KEY, WALLET_WWDR_CERT, WALLET_PASS_TYPE_ID and WALLET_TEAM_ID in the Worker''s secrets); then it shows on every confirmed booking.


Program: **Call and Text buttons go through Quo** (on) makes every Call and Text button use the CarmaCars number in Quo (chapter Texts and calls). Off, they open the device''s own phone and messages apps.

## Stuck? help

**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Stuck? help**: turn it on or off, the minutes on a page without a successful action (3), and the errors (3) before the box offers the guide and the Academy lesson. **Where people get stuck**, on the same page, lists the pages it showed on most in the last 30 days, with how often the guide and the lesson were opened.

### API access (Claude and scripts)

Settings > **API access** connects Claude so you (or Mahad) can run CarmaCars from a Claude chat: bookings, offers, payments, refunds, returns, cars, rates, listings, owners, invoices, staff and hiring ("hire Ana as customer service"). **Connect from Claude**: in Claude, Settings > Connectors > Add custom connector, paste https://carmacars.ca/api/mcp, then sign in to CarmaCars and press **Allow**. Every change is two steps: Claude first shows what will change (nothing is changed yet), and does it only when you agree. Keys and connections made with every scope got the Admin scopes in release 33; a key with fewer scopes keeps them. For Claude Code or a script, **Make a key**: copy it at once, it is shown only once. Each key or connection acts as its Admin, with the scopes chosen; **Revoke** stops it at once. The **Call log** lists every call (the previews too) with the values before and after. The database checks each action exactly as the Admin screens do.

### The logo

The site, every portal, every email and the documents show the brand logo. To use another, upload it under Settings > **Site settings**, the Logo card (PNG or JPEG for emails and documents).

## Deposits stay as holds (release 28)

Every deposit by card is a hold (an authorization) that stays with Stripe: it is never captured by itself, so nothing is paid out and nothing has to be refunded. Capture only what is owed, and release the rest from the booking. The booking''s Security deposit panel shows Hold expires with the date Stripe gives. When a hold nears its expiry while the car is out or tickets can still come in, Finance gets a To do with **Re-authorize the hold**: a new hold on the saved card, then the old one is released.

**Program settings**: **Extended deposit holds (up to about 30 days)** stays off until Stripe confirms IC+ pricing and extended authorization; when on, the hold on the saved card asks for a longer authorization and falls back to a standard one by itself. It never touches the rental payment. Capturing a deposit hold by itself is off. The heavy cleaning fee (an excessively dirty or smoked-in car) is $300 in **Fees**, editable as every fee.

## Updated terms to accept

**Settings** > **Updated terms**. When the terms of use, the privacy policy or an agreement template changes, publish the new version here; with **Requires acceptance** on, each person it binds accepts it before using their portal.

1. Press **Publish a version**. Choose the Document (the terms of use and the privacy policy bind everyone with a portal; each agreement binds the people who sign it: renters, owners, fleet suppliers, partners, investors, or staff and field).
2. Give the Version (for example the date it takes effect) and **What changed**: people read this summary first.
3. Paste **The new text**. For the terms of use or the privacy policy, leave it empty to use the site''s current text; a text you paste also replaces the site''s page.
4. Leave **Requires acceptance** on and press **Publish a version**.
5. Everyone it binds whose account was opened before sees **We''ve updated our terms** full screen on their next visit, with your summary and the text, and presses Accept. The acceptance is recorded with the time, the IP address, the device and the version.
6. **Accepted** on each version opens who accepted it and when.

> Good to know: It is a click-through acceptance of the new version: no signed agreement is voided and no renter signs the agreement of a past booking again. An Admin account is never asked.

> Good to know: Every agreement is signed with the e-signature only (the identity steps, the IP address, the audit trail): a signature on paper is never recorded. Only an official ServiceOntario form, which the government requires signed in ink, is recorded from its scan.

### Card processing fee for a debit deposit
Program settings: **Card processing fee for a debit deposit: percent (hundredths: 290 is 2.9%)** and **Card processing fee for a debit deposit: fixed part (cents)** (30 is $0.30). When a deposit is charged instead of held on a debit or prepaid card, the renter pays this fee on it, as a separate non-refundable amount shown before they pay, on the receipt and on the Money tab. Set both to 0 to charge no fee.

## My profile and name changes (release 34)
Settings > **My profile** has your display name, **Request a name change** for your legal name, your phone number and **Change my password**. When someone else asks to change the legal name on their agreements, it comes to To do with Approve and Decline, and shows on their page (owner, investor or renter). Approving changes the name on their account and record; agreements already signed keep the name they were signed with.', 'Settings', 'Site, program settings, official forms mapping, insurers and the other lists.',
  'Settings change the public site and the rules of the program at once. Program settings are kept as dated rows, so earlier values stay on record.

## The Settings page

1. Site setup lists what is still missing on the public site, with **Open site settings**.
2. Site settings: contact details, hours, tagline, logo, socials, Google place id and featured cars.
3. Program settings: every timing and policy value.
4. Forms: Blind Spot''s rental agreement for every booking, and the official ServiceOntario PDFs and what goes in each field.
5. Insurers: insurance companies billed for bookings.

![](/guides/img/admin-24-settings-desktop-89b31691.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 900; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings; pins: 1 32.6 33.0, 2 25.8 40.2, 3 77.4 40.2, 4 25.8 73.2, 5 25.8 84.9")

The other tiles: Site content (headings, FAQs, legal text), Fee defaults, Deposit tiers, Kilometre choices, Vehicle classes, Vehicle class rules, Airports and delivery, Protection Plan prices, Card coverage, Reviews, Quo contacts (everyone with a phone number as a contact in Quo: see Texts and calls), Text alerts, Partners (each partner company''s CRM link: see Partners, company cars and rentals added by hand), Email aliases and reply-to, My profile, Staff and roles, Promo codes and Quick replies.

**My profile**: the greeting name of this login. To do greets it whole ("Good morning, Abbas and Mahad" on a login the owners share) and the assistant uses it; empty, the first name of the account. Press **Change the greeting name**, type it and save.

## Program settings

1. Buffer between trips (90 minutes): the time held before and after every trip, in every availability and conflict check (requests, offers, date changes, extensions, the calendar). The cleaning block after a trip is this time; Turnaround between trips is the same number. A booking already closer than this is not changed: the calendar rings it.
1. Late fee and extensions (Booking requests and offers): the late fee per started hour (17.5% of the daily rate, at least $25; new bookings and offers only), the extension discounts (5% for a day or more, 10% for 1 or 3 hours) and **Approve a renter''s extension at once when nothing needs a person** (on). A car''s own switch is in Fleet, the car, **Edit details**: **Renters extend themselves**.
2. Settings come in groups such as Company, Booking requests and offers, Owner debits and statement emails, Deposits, Delivery, Owners and fleet, and Tolls and damage. Open one to see its fields.
3. First reply target for customer service and sales (minutes), under Booking requests and offers: 5 by default. New booking requests, enquiries, changes renters ask for and renter messages are due that many minutes after they come in; the scorecard and the staff screens use it. What renters are told (Reply wording, in Site settings) is separate.
4. Staff commissions and prices typed by hand: the commission outside Sales (10%), the three Sales tiers and their days (10%, 15% from 50 days, 20% from 100 days, the month''s target), the price floor a day (empty: none) and the discount from the rate sheet that flags a price (20%). The owner confirmed these values in October 2026. The remote Sales values follow: the three remote tiers (5%, 10%, 15%), the touches a month (400), the drop under it (one tier) and its floor (2.5%), the peak hours a week (20), the reply target (15 minutes) and the peak hours (noon to 6 pm, Thursday to Sunday).
5. Staff agreement defaults by function, at the bottom: pay (a month, an hour or commission only), the rate, the schedule (full time, part time or flexible), days a week and hours a day for Customer service, Fleet, Finance and Sales, the values every assistant shares, and the field staff wage. Sales is commission only: no rate and a flexible schedule. Press **Save the defaults**.
6. Live visitors and live chat: recording visits, the signal thresholds, follow-up tasks, the chat and its assistant, and how long visits and chats are kept.
7. Discount games: the same values as Settings, Discount games (the prize table and the games are easier to change there).
8. Deposits: the toll and ticket window after the return (7 days: settling sooner suggests a hold-back), the longest hold-back (30 days after the return), how long before a card hold lapses it is collected (36 hours), and collecting what is owed after the deposit by itself (the card on file, then a pay link, then a Finance task). A deposit is never released by itself.
9. Field jobs and handovers: field jobs made from each confirmed booking (on) and who gets them (the least busy field staff member, or nobody so Fleet assigns), how field staff may take a deposit at the check-in besides a card (e-Transfer and cash), and whether they may release a car whose tracker is not reporting, with a reason (on; you get an urgent task). Field pay: the first day of a pay period (every period is two weeks), the default hourly rate (CA$18.00), whether overtime is paid (off), after how many hours in a week (44) and at what share of the rate (150%), vacation pay added to each statement (off; Ontario 4%) and the longest shift (16 hours).
10. Sign-in by phone: codes by text from the CarmaCars number (on), US numbers (off until the Quo number is registered for US texting, A2P 10DLC), codes per number and per connection an hour, and whether a verified phone confirms an account like a confirmed email. Accepting an offer, signing and paying need a confirmed account; an account made by phone gives its email on the pay page before its first payment.
11. Calendar sync, Turo by email, Booking recovery emails and Site check: how often calendar links are read, the Turo inbound address and who may forward to it, the reminder delays and sending hours, and the site check with the address its alerts go to (rent@carmacars.ca), the minutes before an email, the daily limit and the quiet hours.
12. Change a value and press **Save**. It is saved as a new row from today; the rows before stay as they were.

![](/guides/img/admin-25-program-settings-desktop-d16b066c.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1000; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings/program; pins: 1 25.8 22.0, 2 27.8 49.0")


## Lead-time pricing

A car booked at short notice costs a little more and one booked well ahead a little less. Open **Settings**, then **Program settings**: Lead-time pricing is at the top.

1. The switch turns it on or off for every car (on by default).
2. The table holds the tiers: when the pickup is that many hours away, the rental charge changes by that percentage. By default: under 24 hours +15%, 24 to 72 hours +10%, 3 to 13 days 0%, 14 days or more −5%. Type the hours and the percentage on each row (a minus for less); **Add a tier** adds one, **Remove** takes one off. Each row shows what it does to a $500 rental.
3. **Also adjust bookings billed to an insurer** is off by default: an insurer pays its own rate, never a short-notice premium.
4. Press **Save lead-time pricing**. New quotes and requests use it; bookings already made keep theirs.

| What it touches | How |
| --- | --- |
| The rental charge | The percentage of the rental charge only, before tax: one line in the price, "Short-notice pricing +10%" or "Booked ahead −5%". Never the fees, the deposit or add-ons |
| When it is worked out | When the quote is made (the car page, the cars list once dates are chosen, the request), from that moment to the pickup on Toronto clocks. "From $X a day" stays at the base rate |
| When it is locked | On the request: the offer, a change of dates and the payment keep the same percentage |
| Other discounts | The non-refundable discount, a promo code and a staff discount are worked out on the rental charge from the rates, as before, and show beside it |
| Owner revenue and commissions | Count the rental charge after it, as they count the discounts |
| Staff | Change it on a booking under **More options** on the review screen; a price typed by hand replaces it. Rentals added by hand, Owner Bookings and placeholders are not adjusted |

> Tip: A car can turn it off or have its own tiers: **Vehicles** > the car > **Rates** > Lead-time pricing for this car.
## Vehicle class rules

Open **Settings**, then **Vehicle class rules**. How a new car''s class is decided from its VIN: the first rule that matches wins.

1. The table lists each rule: its rank, what the car must be (a make, and patterns for the model, the trim and the body), the class it gets, the class once the car is old enough, a note and whether it is on. The lowest rank that matches is used; a car that matches no rule is Standard.
2. Press **Add a rule** or **Change**: a rank, at least one condition, the class, optionally the years old after which an older class applies, and a note (it is shown as the reason for the class). A pattern is not case sensitive: ^911 matches models that start with 911. A rule with no condition, a pattern that does not compile and an older class equal to the class are refused.
3. **Try a car** gives the class the rules decide for a year, make, model, trim and body, and why.
4. **Delete** removes a rule; switch it off instead to keep it. Every add, change and delete is in the audit log, with before and after.

> Tip: A rule changes the cars entered from then on. A car already listed keeps its class until you change it on the car.

## Official ServiceOntario forms

The five official forms are loaded with a mapping to the owner, car, company and lender details. Each is the form exactly as ServiceOntario publishes it: only its empty text boxes are filled; its own text and layout are never changed. A form whose stored PDF is not the publisher''s download (or your upload of it) gives owners the data sheet instead. Its checkboxes, drop-downs and signatures are done by hand at the counter, in ink. Until you check a form, owners get a data sheet with the values.

1. Open **Settings** > **Forms**. Each form shows "Mapping to check" (a draft is ready) or "Official PDF in use". Its notes say what the form is for and which boxes are left blank on purpose.
2. Choose **Preview with**: a sample car (made-up values) or one of the cars. Press **Download a filled preview** and check each value against the form. The preview uses the mapping on screen, saved or not.
3. Change a field if needed: What goes in it (or "Signed here by hand, in ink"), a Format (for example YYYY/MM/DD) and Only when. Write what you changed and press Save the mapping. **Earlier mappings** lists every save, with who and when; **Load** puts one back on screen to preview and save again. Fleet can map the forms too (Owners > Government forms), but only an Admin uploads a form.
4. Press **Checked: use for owners**. Every owner''s form of that kind is filled again, except ones already signed or filed. Owners download it, print it and sign it in ink; record it with **Record an official form signed in ink**. Each form not checked yet is also a line on To do with the same button and Preview it.
5. A new version from ServiceOntario? Press **Upload the official fillable PDF**: the fields of the same name keep their mapping.

> Good to know: SR-LV-006 (registration), SR-LV-012 (two registrants), ON00453 (a company''s RIN), 013-1155 and 013-0169 (the tax-exempt transfer into an owner''s corporation). 013-1155 is sworn before a commissioner, so it is printed and signed in person. ON00453 is an Adobe form: it opens in Adobe Acrobat Reader. Each form''s notes list what to tick or choose at the counter. A car gets only the forms its onboarding method needs: no form for a Transfer of a car owned outright or financed (the sign-back on the permit), 013-1155 and 013-0169 only for a Lease through a new Owner Corporation.

## Blind Spot rental agreement

We rent under Blind Spot Car Rental''s insurance, so every booking has two agreements: CarmaCars'' rental agreement and Blind Spot''s own. Blind Spot''s is filled in from the booking, the renter and the car, and the renter signs both with one signature. Its PDF is stored privately, never on the website.

1. Open **Settings** > **Forms**. The Blind Spot Car Rental agreement card is first. Press **Upload Blind Spot''s PDF** and choose Blind Spot''s blank form (2 pages, A4).
2. Press **Download the filled sample**: a made-up booking on the form. **Sample billed to an insurer** also fills the claim number, the adjuster and the insurance company. Check every box.
3. On the form the old address (top left and twice in box 15) is replaced by the mailing address of Site settings, box 1 by CarmaCars'' HST number (Program settings, Company HST number; blank until it is entered), and box 21 has the representative''s signature instead of Sam''s.
4. Press **Checked: use for bookings**. From then on each booking gets it when its rental agreement is made; a renter whose agreement is already open gets it the next time they open the signing page.
5. Box 21: Ahmad is written in a script hand, as Blind Spot asked. To use a real signature instead, upload a PNG under Authorized company representative; Remove the image goes back to the written name. Full name is for the signature record page.
6. A new version of Blind Spot''s form? Upload it the same way: it waits for **Checked: use for bookings**, and bookings keep the version in use until then.

> Good to know: Each box is filled only when the booking has the value: the renter and their licence, the additional drivers, the car (plate, make and model, the fleet number as vehicle number), the pickup as time and date out, the due-back date and time, the kilometres allowed, the rate rows (days, weeks or months @ the rate = the amount; a rental counted by the day, such as 31 days at the monthly rate, shows its daily rate rounded to the cent, and box 14 says how the charge was made), the underage fee, the Protection Plan as CDW, winter tires, the subtotal, HST (13% of the subtotal), total and deposit, the deposit received and the day it was taken (before pickup, the amount due at pickup), and for a booking billed to an insurer the insurer, claim number and adjuster. Other charges, such as delivery, are listed in box 14. The boxes filled at check-in and check-out stay blank until then. The fuel gauges are covered and the level of the check-in report (fuel out) and the check-out report (fuel in) is written in words, blank with no reading.

The renter''s signature goes in boxes 16, 17 and 20 of the signed copy, with the day they signed beside box 20 and a signature record page. Each later version (as picked up, as returned, corrected) carries the same signature and day. Both agreements are in the booking''s Drivers and documents tab, in the renter''s Documents, and the signed Blind Spot agreement is attached to the "Your signed rental agreement" email. Admin > Today lists the HST number, the upload and the check until they are done.

## Agreements to sign: investors and staff

Investment agreements and staff agreements are made from the person''s record and signed in their own portal, with the e-signature (never on paper).

1. Investor: open **People** > **Investors** and the investor. Under Investment agreement, press **Send the agreement to sign**. Check the values it is filled with (amount, yearly percentage, dates, exemption) and press **Send to sign**.
2. Once the investor signs, the agreement shows **Awaiting countersignature** on the investor''s page and on To do. It is not countersigned automatically: check it and press **Countersign**. CarmaCars is bound once it has countersigned and the funds clear.
3. Staff: open **People** > **Team**. Under Staff agreements, press **Send the agreement to sign** beside the person. Pay, schedule, hours and the other values start from the staff profile and the defaults of their function in Program settings; change any before sending. For Sales the Pay is Commission only: the agreement then has no rate, schedule or hours, and pays the commission of section 3.4.
4. A field staff member''s agreement prints the home address they entered themselves. Staff enter their home address at their first sign-in, before they sign, or in their profile.
5. They get a notice, check the key values and sign in their portal in a few taps (their name is the signature, or they draw it). The signed copy is filed with their documents.
6. Your own PDF instead? **Send a PDF to sign** still works.
7. Sent by mistake? Press **Withdraw** and give the reason.

## The user guides

**Settings** > **Guides**. The guide of each portal, as people read it under Guide.

1. Each guide shows its version, when it was published and whether there are unpublished changes.
2. Open a guide and press a section. Change its text and press **Show the preview** to see it as people will. Press **Save the draft**; each save is kept in the section''s history.
3. Move a section with the arrows, hide it, or press **Add a chapter**. Upload a screenshot under Screenshots and paste the line it gives you.
4. Press **Publish version** (the next number). The portals show the new version at once.
5. The stored PDF is printed again by the guides-pdf workflow. Until then the guide says the web guide has newer edits.

## The guides keep up by themselves

After every update of the site that changes the portals, the guides are checked without anyone asking.

1. Every screenshot is taken again on the new version of the site. One whose screen changed replaces the old one in the guide.
2. The text of each section whose screen changed, or that names a button the portals no longer show, is rewritten from the portal''s own labels and menu, checked, and published. The PDFs of those guides are printed again.
3. Such a section says **Changed automatically on** and the date, in the list of guides and in the guide''s editor. Not right? Open the section and press **Revert**: the text it replaced comes back, published at once.
4. This includes sections you edited: the newest automatic text is published, and every earlier version stays in the section''s history. There is nothing to review.
5. A rewrite that does not pass the checks is asked again, more strictly. If it still does not pass, the screenshots and button names are updated, the rest of the text stays as it was, and the next run tries again.

> Tip: The card "The guides keep up by themselves" at the top of Guides lists the last runs: when, how many screenshots were replaced, how many sections were rewritten, and how many PDFs were printed.

## Insurers and the other lists

1. Open Insurers. Each insurer on file opens to edit its billing contact, email, phone, address and notes. Its rates by car class are in **Money** > **Insurers**.
2. To add one, fill in the Add form (Name, Billing contact, Billing email and the rest) and press **Add**.
3. Deposit tiers, Kilometre choices, Vehicle classes, Airports, Promo codes and Quick replies work the same way.

## Promo codes: end dates and reminders

**Settings**, **Promo codes**.

- Every code made for a person has an end date: a game prize 7 days, a come-back offer 30, a Live visitors code 3 and a code made for one renter 30 unless you set another. The first card of Promo codes holds the 30 days and the two reminders.
- A code for everyone may have no end date: empty Valid until. The Add form starts with an end date 30 days ahead.
- A code that ended is refused wherever it is typed (the request form, an offer, Add a rental, a booking edit) with "This code has expired".
- A person who has not used a code is reminded 3 days before its last day and the day before, by email and by text as they chose, never once they used it, unsubscribed or the code ended, and never twice. A game code reminder always goes; a reminder of any other code needs their consent to offers.
- The list shows each code''s end date and the reminders sent. The card Codes sent to people lists game prizes, come-back offers and Live visitors codes the same way.

## Card coverage: which credit cards include rental car coverage

**Settings** > **Card coverage** is the list renters see at `carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage` and staff see under Card coverage in their portal. It starts filled in with 48 Canadian and US cards, each checked on October 23, 2026.

1. The table shows each card: who pays first (Primary, Secondary, or not stated), the car value limit (MSRP), the longest rental, whether the numbers were read in the issuer''s own document, and when it was last checked.
2. Open a card under Change a card, open its official guide, correct what changed and press **Save**. Changing the facts without a date marks the card checked today; type a Last checked date to record another day.
3. A card whose numbers come from a published summary has Read in the issuer''s own document unticked and the summary''s link under Where the numbers came from. The page shows it as Unverified. Tick it once you have read the issuer''s guide.
4. Add a card with the Add form; untick Shown to hide one. Changes reach the public page at once.

> Tip: A card not checked for 6 months shows on Today until it is checked again. The page tells renters to confirm with their card issuer and says CarmaCars decides no claims: keep the list to facts from the issuer''s guide.

## Reviews: review requests and Google

**Settings** > **Reviews**: when review requests go, the Google review link and the Google Business Profile connection. Review requests are on from the start.

1. When review requests go: the check-out (on or off, the shortest rental, hours after the pickup), the request (minutes after the check-out), the reminder (hours) and the final follow-up (days), the sending hours (9 am to 9 pm), and the hold while charges are open.
2. The Google review link: the Google place id (Site settings) makes it, or paste the Business Profile''s own review link.
3. Google Business Profile: press **Connect Google** and sign in with rent@carmacars.ca, then allow access. Reviews are read every 6 hours and matched to renters by name within 30 days after their return.
4. A clear match stops that renter''s reminders at once. A possible match waits in Reviews: press **Confirm**, **Not this renter** or **Match to a booking**.

> Tip: Until Google approves the Business Profile API for the project, the status says so and nothing else changes: renters still get the review link, and "I already left a review", Mark reviewed and on-site reviews still stop the messages.

### Pair the card reader
**Settings** > **Card reader**. On the Stripe S700, swipe from the left edge, open **Settings**, then **Generate pairing code**. Type the three words in **Pairing code**, name the reader (Front desk) and press **Pair reader**. The first time, a Stripe Terminal location is made from the mailing address in Site settings: write it as street, city, province and postal code. **Remove** takes a reader off the list. Card statements read 18122211 Canada Inc., the Stripe account''s statement descriptor.

### Rewards
**Settings** > **Rewards**. CarmaCars Rewards is on: 1 point per dollar of the rental charge after discounts (never fees, add-ons, coverage, tax or the deposit), 100 points = $1, redeemed from 500 points as a code of the renter''s own, valid 90 days. Points end 12 months after the last rental or redemption, with a reminder email 30 days before.

1. **Ways to earn**: each on or off with its points. Referral (500 to the referrer, 250 to the friend, at the friend''s first completed rental), a follow on Instagram, TikTok or Facebook (50 each, once, granted on the click from the Rewards page, since a follow cannot be checked; a platform shows only with its page in Site settings), a review on carmacars.ca (100, any rating; the review shows "Received reward points"), a Google review (100 a rental, any rating, on the renter''s word: they press I posted my review and give the name on it; hidden until the Google review page is set here), a damage-free rental (200: no damage, claim, cleaning or smoking fee, back on time), the birthday (100) and the first rental (100).
2. **Tiers**: Member, Silver from 10 rental days in 12 months (5% off) and Gold from 30 (10% off), with a perk staff honour on request. The discount is a promo code of the renter''s own.
3. Points, tier discounts and codes come off the rental charge only and reduce Owner Revenue like any promo code.
4. **Google reviews claimed** lists every claim; **Reverse** takes the points back with a reason. **A renter''s points**: find the renter, then **Add or take off points** with a reason, or reverse any entry (for example, referral fraud).

