An urgent To do "The renter says the car is back" means the renter pressed **I''ve returned the car** on an overdue booking. Their overdue notices are paused. Open the booking, check the car (place, tracker, the renter''s photos), then press **Confirm** (correct the odometer, fuel or time first if needed; the trip is completed) or **Deny** with the reason (the renter is told and the notices start again).

**Start a listing** takes the VIN from the car: **Scan the barcode** in the door frame or under the windshield, or **Photo of the VIN**.

**Add photos** on a listing takes any number of photos at once, in any order: each is sorted to its shot. A photo that fits no shot goes in with **Extra outside photos** or **Extra inside and detail photos**; drag the extras into their order in the review and press **Save the order**. 10 photos and one outside photo complete the listing. Outside photos are framed big on the studio floor with a shadow under the tyres; a watermark or caption at a photo''s edge is cut off by itself. **Cover the plate** opens with the plate box suggested: check it and save. A car small in the frame, or no model name behind it: press **Frame the outside photos again** (then check the plates again). A bad cut-out (a mirror missing, background left): press **Edit the cut-out**, erase or restore with the brush, move or size the car on the studio, then **Save as a new version**. The version before is kept; if the car did not move, the plate check carries over. Every photo gets a light touch-up by itself; tick **Use original colours** under a photo to make it again without it. Outside photos go in the dark CarmaCars showroom (the logo on the wall, the model''s name behind the car on the cover). A car still on the black studio: press **Apply showroom to this car**; **Listings** > **Apply showroom to every car** does every car. Under a photo, **Redo** makes it again and **Back to the original** puts back the version before. **Marketing photos** on a listing makes copies in other scenes for Marketplace and social posts (choose a scene or **Mix: a different scene on each photo**, then **Make the marketing set**); the website''s photos stay as they are. **First photo** on a listing chooses what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit: **Plain car**, **With a model** (the image model''s car-show photo, a fully clothed adult model beside the car) or **Flyer** (the price a day from the live rates, the call to action and the logo on the cover). Switch any time; until the chosen one is made the plain cover shows.
## One screen, many photos (release 28)

**Import photos from a Google Drive link** on a listing adds the photos of a public Drive folder to the car, sorted and processed like Add photos. **Listings** > **Import photos from Drive** reads a whole folder of folders (one per make, then per car), proposes the car for each folder, and imports once you confirm the table. The page follows the import and ends with what was imported, skipped and failed, and why. The same Drive file is never added twice. Customer service can import into a car whose listing is already started; Fleet and Admin can start one.

Check-in and check-out are one screen on the booking page: the time, km, fuel, many photos at once (tag angles if you like) and a note. The renter''s own photos join the same report; each photo shows who took it. On a car''s page, record **Pickup from owner** and **Return to owner** with photos: the owner sees them.

## Repair costs on a car

On a car''s page, **Kickbacks and repairs** lists its repair costs and the kickbacks partners paid on it. **Add a repair cost**: the date, the shop or another vendor, what was done, the amount and tax, who paid (CarmaCars, the owner or the insurer), the claim and a photo or PDF of the receipt.

## When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)
On the booking page, **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking''s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: **Ask to record a past trip** with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.

## Incident cards (release 34)
**Cars**, then **Incident cards**, prints the card for the visor or the glovebox: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, our support and roadside numbers, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. On a car''s page, **Incident card** prints that car; on the list, **Print all cars** prints every car, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks. Laminate it and put one in each car. The insurance policy on the card is set by an Admin; until it is, the card tells the renter to ask for the slip. No price is ever printed on it.

## Government forms (release 35)
The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner''s car are on the owner''s page and the car''s page, under **Government forms**. Open a form, press **Change a value**, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and **Save**: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under **Versions** with their downloads. **Back to the records** undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. **Make again** keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. **Owners**, then **Government forms**, opens the forms'' mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under **Earlier mappings**. Only the boxes are filled: the form''s own text and layout never change.

## Odometer and fuel at every check-in and check-out

Every check-in and check-out on one screen asks for two photos besides the others:

1. **Photo of the dashboard**: the odometer and the fuel gauge, from the camera roll or the camera. The site reads it and asks, for example, "Odometer 45,210 km, fuel 3/4: correct?". Press **Yes, correct**, or **No, I will type it** and type the odometer and pick the fuel in eighths.
2. **Selfie in front of the car**: taken now with the camera, never from the camera roll. A selfie without a fresh capture time is noted on the report for you to check; it never stops the check-in.

At the return the site compares with the pickup: km driven, km over the included allowance and the fuel difference. The extra km (the booking''s rate per km) and the fuel (the refill price per eighth) are added to the booking by themselves. The photo report shows both dashboard photos side by side with the readings and these charges.

## Change the car of a confirmed booking

A car with a problem before pickup? On the booking, press **Change the car**, choose a car free for the dates and say why. The price comes from the new car''s rate sheet; more to pay is left open for the renter, less becomes a refund for approval. The jobs move to the new car and the renter gets one email.

## An accident reported by a renter

A renter can report an accident from the accident card on their booking. It opens the incident with its first-response steps and your To do, and sends you an urgent alert (on duty) and to Admins: what happened, where, the photos and videos, the other party, the police report number, whether anyone is hurt and whether the car can be driven. Call the renter at once; a car that cannot be driven is already out of service with its calendar blocked.
## Payments and calls (release 35)
Fleet takes payments on a booking''s **Money** tab: text or email a pay link, charge the saved card when the renter agreed, hold the deposit, or record cash or an e-Transfer received (within your single limit; Finance gets a To do to check it). Refunds, captures and voids stay with Finance and the Admins.

Calls and texts about pickups, returns, deliveries and cars on rent come to Fleet first: the caller pop-up shows them, and **More fleet** > **Calls and texts** is your inbox. A car late back has **Returning now** on its late panel: press it when the renter says they are on the way, and they get no more overdue reminders for that return time.

The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner''s car are on the owner''s page and the car''s page, under **Government forms**. Open a form, press **Change a value**, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and **Save**: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under **Versions** with their downloads. **Back to the records** undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. **Make again** keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. **Owners**, then **Government forms**, opens the forms'' mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under **Earlier mappings**. Only the boxes are filled: the form''s own text and layout never change. The owner signs each form on screen: the page shows **Owner''s signature** beside the form (who, when, the version) and **Download the print-ready form** has no signature on it. A value changed after signing shows **Changed since signed** and the owner is asked to sign again.

## Close ended trips

A back-dated close sends the renter no email or text. Fleet gets a To do when a trip is still open 2 hours after its return time, and the morning digest lists how many are open.

**Field jobs** > **Close ended trips**: tick the trips that ended and were never closed, mark them returned on time or late (with the time), choose the deposit decision (deduct the balance owed, deduct the late fee, or release in full) and press **Close**. An expired card hold is settled by expiry at once. An Admin presses Release for the rest. On a booking, an expired hold after the return has **Mark settled (released by expiry)**.

## Field applicant calls (release 35)

Field applicants who pass the AI interview book a 10-minute live call in the hour before the weekly townhall. **Field applicant calls** on your home page lists the six slots and who took each one.',
  '<p class="gd-p">You keep the cars moving: field jobs, daily checks, photo reviews after returns, and the listings with their duplicate check and plate covering.</p><p class="gd-p">Your rail: Queue, Today, Field jobs, Field hours, Daily checks, Photo reviews, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Find a renter and Scorecard.</p><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-schedule-field-jobs" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Schedule field jobs</h2><p class="gd-p">Every confirmed booking gets its handover (or delivery) and return (or pickup) jobs by itself, at the booking&#39;s times and place, and put on a shift: the shift covering its time, or that day&#39;s (see Shifts and who gets a job). The people on the shift share its jobs, least busy first. You check and change them.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Jobs, next three days: each with its place, its shift, its field staff and whether they acknowledged it. &quot;Made from the booking&quot; marks the ones made by themselves; when the booking moves, they move too, unless you changed them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Change a job with <b class="gd-ui">To a shift</b> (another shift), <b class="gd-ui">Assign</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Reassign</b> (a field person on a shift that day when the day has shifts, or an Admin), <b class="gd-ui">Move</b> (time and place) or <b class="gd-ui">Cancel</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Handovers and returns without a job (when the automatic jobs are off, or one was cancelled) are listed first: press <b class="gd-ui">Schedule</b>, the place filled in from the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An Admin turns the automatic jobs or the assignment off in Settings &gt; Program.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/fleet</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/565"><img src="/guides/img/va-fleet-02-field-jobs-desktop-8e721230.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="565"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:17.9%;top:51.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-shifts-and-who-gets-a-job" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Shifts and who gets a job</h2><p class="gd-p">Field staff take their shifts from a schedule you publish, ideally a week ahead. A job is given by itself only to a field person who passed the academy and holds a shift that day, and work lands only on days with shifts.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On <b class="gd-ui">Field jobs</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Shifts, next seven days</b> shows each day and how many people are on a shift, and each shift its jobs (<b class="gd-ui">Jobs on it</b>). A shift with jobs and nobody on it is marked; within 24 hours of its start you get an alert and a To do, once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Publish shifts</b>: the first day&#39;s start and end, how many people, and for how many days the same hours repeat. Field staff take them on their phones.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a person</b> puts someone on a shift and <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes them off. A person who has not passed the academy cannot take shifts or be given a job.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A shift nobody claimed keeps its jobs: field staff see them when they look for shifts to claim, and the one who claims it gets them. A shift given up or swapped takes its jobs along; a cancelled shift sends them to another shift.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Work due on a day with no shifts moves to the day before when it is known in advance, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day. The job shows its planned day and keeps the booking&#39;s real time; the renter&#39;s times never change. A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning: cover it, or move the booking time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Unassign</b> takes a job off its person and its shift; tick <b class="gd-ui">Tell them</b> only if they should know. The Admins can be given a job too (no shift needed).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-fleet-map" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fleet map</h2><p class="gd-p">At the top of <b class="gd-ui">Field jobs</b>: every car on the map with its renter, booking, due-back time and state, the alerts, and the trips by booking, the same as the Admin&#39;s. Only Admins and fleet staff see positions.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press a car for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery and the trip under way.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">An alert (speeding, left Ontario or the zone, still driving after the return time, low or unplugged tracker, not reporting) also comes to your bell and as an urgent phone alert. Call the renter, then press <b class="gd-ui">Seen</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car still driving after its return time: call, send the late notice and offer a paid extension, as for any late return.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-field-hours" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Field hours</h2><p class="gd-p">Field staff clock in and out on their phones. You see who is clocked in and every shift of the two-week pay period, and you fix what they cannot.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Field hours</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Clocked in now</b> lists who is on, since when. <b class="gd-ui">Earlier period</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Later period</b> move between pay periods.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Someone forgot to clock out: press <b class="gd-ui">Clock out for them</b>, set the time they finished and write the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Someone forgot to clock in, or a time is wrong: <b class="gd-ui">Add hours</b> enters a shift, <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> fixes one and <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes one out. Each needs a reason; the change is kept in a log with what it was before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Once an Admin approves the pay run of a period, its shifts are locked: ask the Admin. You see hours only, not rates or pay.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Where they clocked in</h3><p class="gd-p">The hours list shows where each person clocked in and out: a map link and the distance from the lot. A clock in or out over 500 m away, or with the location refused, is shown in bold with the reason the person wrote. Their location is asked only at those two moments, never in between.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-daily-checks" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Daily checks</h2><p class="gd-p">Twice a day: the opening check by 9:00 and the closing check by 18:00.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Daily checks</b> and choose <b class="gd-ui">Opening check</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Closing check</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each line shows what was found. Tick OK, or Problem with a note.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the opening check</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Save the closing check</b>). You can save it again.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/checks</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/820"><img src="/guides/img/va-fleet-03-daily-checks-desktop-be06d6c0.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="820"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:6.5%;top:15.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:44.7%;top:42%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:64.2%;top:94%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-check-a-car-out-or-in" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check a car out or in</h2><p class="gd-p">Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in from the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a confirmed booking press <b class="gd-ui">Check in (pickup)</b>; on a booking on rent, <b class="gd-ui">Check out (return)</b>. Today lists the ones due, each with its button.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The checklist field staff use opens: readings (km and fuel or charge), the photo set with the plate and the gauges, damage close-ups and both signatures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Afterwards press <b class="gd-ui">Photo report</b>: times, Late by, kilometres, fuel, photos and the return charges. Fleet waives a charge with <b class="gd-ui">Waive</b> and a reason.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-photo-reviews-after-a-return" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Photo reviews after a return</h2><p class="gd-p">After each return, the field photo set waits under <b class="gd-ui">Photo reviews</b>. Compare it with the pickup set. Press <b class="gd-ui">Review done</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Ask for a re-shoot</b> if a photo is missing or unclear.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-similar-cars" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Similar cars</h2><p class="gd-p">A possible duplicate never keeps a car off the site: it shows on the car&#39;s checklist until you decide. Only Same car takes it off.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each flag shows the car, what it looks like (same VIN, plate, photo or specs) and the other car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Compare the permit, the plate and the photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Not a duplicate</b> with a note when they are different cars, or <b class="gd-ui">Same car</b> when they are.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/similar-cars</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/460"><img src="/guides/img/va-fleet-06-similar-cars-desktop-562b0382.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="460"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:23.6%;top:30.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:94.8%;top:30.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-rates-and-kilometres" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rates and kilometres</h2><p class="gd-p">From a listing, press <b class="gd-ui">The car and its rates</b>, or open the car from Field jobs and its <b class="gd-ui">Rates &amp; fees</b> tab.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type the rates an Admin set. Only the daily rate is needed; the others follow from it when empty. The weekend rate is a price per day for each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Keep <b class="gd-ui">Use the defaults</b> for the kilometres, or choose <b class="gd-ui">Custom for this car</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check What renters pay under the fields, then press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rates</b>. Rates, kilometres and deposit save together.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-listings-and-covering-plates" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Listings and covering plates</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>. A draft waiting shows Needs review. Open it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The copy is written by itself (change a line only if you must: it is then kept). Check the photos: on each public photo, cover the plate or mark it not visible.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/listings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/340"><img src="/guides/img/va-fleet-05-listings-desktop-d2672e0a.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="340"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:54.5%;top:49.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol" start="3"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The listing&#39;s Steps to go live says what is next: 1 Photos, 2 Cover plates, 3 Review, 4 Live on the site, each with its button. The plate box is suggested by itself on every outside photo as the listing opens (Box suggested). Press <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b> and check it; <b class="gd-ui">Suggest the plate</b> asks again. A photo filed under the wrong shot: <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> under it on the Photos card, then take the right one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Drag over a plate to draw a box; drag a box to move it, its corner to resize it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Keep <b class="gd-ui">The CARMA Ontario plate</b> on a rear plate or <b class="gd-ui">Edit the front plate out</b> on a front photo (or choose <b class="gd-ui">A CarmaCars plate</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Pixelation</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Blur</b>), then <b class="gd-ui">Save the covered photo</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">No plate in the shot? <b class="gd-ui">No plate visible on this photo</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/776"><img src="/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-phone-95d5afd2.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="776"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:52.6%;top:78.9%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50%;top:43.8%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:61.5%;top:62.1%" aria-hidden="true">5</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:43.1%;top:92.3%" aria-hidden="true">6</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>The plate check never holds a car back: a photo whose plate is not checked stays private, and goes public by itself once it is covered or marked. The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-publish-now" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish now</h2><p class="gd-p">Customer service and fleet publish a car themselves; nothing has to be finished first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the car from Listings or Field jobs. Its listing says why it is not on the site yet; press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>. With no rates yet it uses the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">What is still open (paperwork, details, photos, No VIN yet for a car added by its plate, a possible duplicate) shows as warnings after Publish now and on the car. None of them stops publishing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">New cars with their rates usually go on the site by themselves (Publish new cars automatically, on by default). A car taken off the site by staff waits for Publish now.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A car not on the fleet insurance policy yet can be requested, offered and paid for, but never handed over until the insurer confirms it. Requests and offers for such a car show a warning.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-calendar-sync-with-turo-and-other-platforms" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calendar sync with Turo and other platforms</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Calendar sync</b>: a car listed on Turo or Getaround must never be booked twice.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Turo has no calendar link: Turo&#39;s trip emails come in by themselves, find their car by themselves (Turo car number, plate, VIN, year, make, model, trim, colour, what earlier emails taught) and block it with the turnaround. Nothing to set up per car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">An email the reader cannot place waits as &quot;Which car is this?&quot;: press <b class="gd-ui">Which car is this?</b> and press the right car (best guesses first). It is remembered for that car&#39;s next emails. If the dates or trip number are missing: <b class="gd-ui">Add as a Turo trip</b> (choose the car, check the dates) or <b class="gd-ui">Dismiss</b>. A trip whose email did not come: <b class="gd-ui">Add a Turo trip</b> on the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each Turo trip shows the guest&#39;s name and phone when Turo&#39;s email includes them. Contact a Turo guest only about their trip, never with promotions.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Turo cannot read our calendar: under &quot;Block on Turo&quot;, block each CarmaCars booking on the car&#39;s Turo calendar, then press <b class="gd-ui">Done on Turo</b>. Dates that changed or a booking cancelled here show the dates to free on Turo.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Getaround, Google Calendar or another platform with a calendar (iCal) link: open <b class="gd-ui">Add a calendar link</b>, choose the platform, paste it and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the link</b>. Copy the car&#39;s CarmaCars link for that platform with <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b> and paste it into the platform&#39;s calendar import.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A double booking raises an urgent task for you and an email: move, swap or cancel one trip. A link that stops working raises a task after 3 failed reads: copy it from the platform again.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Add the photos and readings</h3><p class="gd-p">A pickup or return recorded with the details later gives Fleet the task <b class="gd-ui">Add the photos and readings for CC-...</b>. Open the booking and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the check-in (or check-out) photos and readings</b>: the usual checklist opens without the ready check or the renter&#39;s signature. Take the photos, the odometer, fuel, keys (and cleanliness at a return), sign and save. The task closes by itself; it cannot be closed by hand before.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-bookings-now" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Bookings now</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Rentals</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> opens on Now for fleet and customer service: the cars out with their renter and due-back countdown, coming back today and tomorrow (overdue first, in red), going out in the next 72 hours with what is ready, the money due in 7 days and the free cars. It refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. A booking listed as <b class="gd-ui">Out (pickup not recorded)</b> left without a check-in: press <b class="gd-ui">Mark picked up</b>, then add the photos, km and fuel from the task. A car overdue or due back today has <b class="gd-ui">Returned</b> (here, on Today and at the top of the booking): give the return time (now, or earlier; the late charges follow it) and the km and fuel if known. The overdue messages stop and the task for the photos is yours. The search above it finds any booking.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">The renter says the car is back</h3><p class="gd-p">An urgent To do &quot;The renter says the car is back&quot; means the renter pressed <b class="gd-ui">I&#39;ve returned the car</b> on an overdue booking. Their overdue notices are paused. Open the booking, check the car (place, tracker, the renter&#39;s photos), then press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b> (correct the odometer, fuel or time first if needed; the trip is completed) or <b class="gd-ui">Deny</b> with the reason (the renter is told and the notices start again).</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> takes the VIN from the car: <b class="gd-ui">Scan the barcode</b> in the door frame or under the windshield, or <b class="gd-ui">Photo of the VIN</b>.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> on a listing takes any number of photos at once, in any order: each is sorted to its shot. A photo that fits no shot goes in with <b class="gd-ui">Extra outside photos</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Extra inside and detail photos</b>; drag the extras into their order in the review and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the order</b>. 10 photos and one outside photo complete the listing. Outside photos are framed big on the studio floor with a shadow under the tyres; a watermark or caption at a photo&#39;s edge is cut off by itself. <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b> opens with the plate box suggested: check it and save. A car small in the frame, or no model name behind it: press <b class="gd-ui">Frame the outside photos again</b> (then check the plates again). A bad cut-out (a mirror missing, background left): press <b class="gd-ui">Edit the cut-out</b>, erase or restore with the brush, move or size the car on the studio, then <b class="gd-ui">Save as a new version</b>. The version before is kept; if the car did not move, the plate check carries over. Every photo gets a light touch-up by itself; tick <b class="gd-ui">Use original colours</b> under a photo to make it again without it. Outside photos go in the dark CarmaCars showroom (the logo on the wall, the model&#39;s name behind the car on the cover). A car still on the black studio: press <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to this car</b>; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to every car</b> does every car. Under a photo, <b class="gd-ui">Redo</b> makes it again and <b class="gd-ui">Back to the original</b> puts back the version before. <b class="gd-ui">Marketing photos</b> on a listing makes copies in other scenes for Marketplace and social posts (choose a scene or <b class="gd-ui">Mix: a different scene on each photo</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Make the marketing set</b>); the website&#39;s photos stay as they are. <b class="gd-ui">First photo</b> on a listing chooses what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit: <b class="gd-ui">Plain car</b>, <b class="gd-ui">With a model</b> (the image model&#39;s car-show photo, a fully clothed adult model beside the car) or <b class="gd-ui">Flyer</b> (the price a day from the live rates, the call to action and the logo on the cover). Switch any time; until the chosen one is made the plain cover shows.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-one-screen-many-photos-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">One screen, many photos (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Import photos from a Google Drive link</b> on a listing adds the photos of a public Drive folder to the car, sorted and processed like Add photos. <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Import photos from Drive</b> reads a whole folder of folders (one per make, then per car), proposes the car for each folder, and imports once you confirm the table. The page follows the import and ends with what was imported, skipped and failed, and why. The same Drive file is never added twice. Customer service can import into a car whose listing is already started; Fleet and Admin can start one.</p><p class="gd-p">Check-in and check-out are one screen on the booking page: the time, km, fuel, many photos at once (tag angles if you like) and a note. The renter&#39;s own photos join the same report; each photo shows who took it. On a car&#39;s page, record <b class="gd-ui">Pickup from owner</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Return to owner</b> with photos: the owner sees them.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-repair-costs-on-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Repair costs on a car</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Kickbacks and repairs</b> lists its repair costs and the kickbacks partners paid on it. <b class="gd-ui">Add a repair cost</b>: the date, the shop or another vendor, what was done, the amount and tax, who paid (CarmaCars, the owner or the insurer), the claim and a photo or PDF of the receipt.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-when-a-check-stops-the-pickup-or-the-return-release-33" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking page, <b class="gd-ui">What stops the pickup now</b> (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press <b class="gd-ui">Ask an Admin to override the pickup</b> (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking&#39;s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: <b class="gd-ui">Ask to record a past trip</b> with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-incident-cards-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Incident cards (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Incident cards</b>, prints the card for the visor or the glovebox: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, our support and roadside numbers, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Incident card</b> prints that car; on the list, <b class="gd-ui">Print all cars</b> prints every car, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks. Laminate it and put one in each car. The insurance policy on the card is set by an Admin; until it is, the card tells the renter to ask for the slip. No price is ever printed on it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-government-forms-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Government forms (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner&#39;s car are on the owner&#39;s page and the car&#39;s page, under <b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>. Open a form, press <b class="gd-ui">Change a value</b>, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under <b class="gd-ui">Versions</b> with their downloads. <b class="gd-ui">Back to the records</b> undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. <b class="gd-ui">Make again</b> keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Discard the values changed by hand</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>, opens the forms&#39; mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under <b class="gd-ui">Earlier mappings</b>. Only the boxes are filled: the form&#39;s own text and layout never change.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-odometer-and-fuel-at-every-check-in-and-check-out" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Odometer and fuel at every check-in and check-out</h2><p class="gd-p">Every check-in and check-out on one screen asks for two photos besides the others:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Photo of the dashboard</b>: the odometer and the fuel gauge, from the camera roll or the camera. The site reads it and asks, for example, &quot;Odometer 45,210 km, fuel 3/4: correct?&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Yes, correct</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">No, I will type it</b> and type the odometer and pick the fuel in eighths.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Selfie in front of the car</b>: taken now with the camera, never from the camera roll. A selfie without a fresh capture time is noted on the report for you to check; it never stops the check-in.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">At the return the site compares with the pickup: km driven, km over the included allowance and the fuel difference. The extra km (the booking&#39;s rate per km) and the fuel (the refill price per eighth) are added to the booking by themselves. The photo report shows both dashboard photos side by side with the readings and these charges.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-change-the-car-of-a-confirmed-booking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change the car of a confirmed booking</h2><p class="gd-p">A car with a problem before pickup? On the booking, press <b class="gd-ui">Change the car</b>, choose a car free for the dates and say why. The price comes from the new car&#39;s rate sheet; more to pay is left open for the renter, less becomes a refund for approval. The jobs move to the new car and the renter gets one email.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-an-accident-reported-by-a-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An accident reported by a renter</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter can report an accident from the accident card on their booking. It opens the incident with its first-response steps and your To do, and sends you an urgent alert (on duty) and to Admins: what happened, where, the photos and videos, the other party, the police report number, whether anyone is hurt and whether the car can be driven. Call the renter at once; a car that cannot be driven is already out of service with its calendar blocked.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-payments-and-calls-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payments and calls (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Fleet takes payments on a booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab: text or email a pay link, charge the saved card when the renter agreed, hold the deposit, or record cash or an e-Transfer received (within your single limit; Finance gets a To do to check it). Refunds, captures and voids stay with Finance and the Admins.</p><p class="gd-p">Calls and texts about pickups, returns, deliveries and cars on rent come to Fleet first: the caller pop-up shows them, and <b class="gd-ui">More fleet</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Calls and texts</b> is your inbox. A car late back has <b class="gd-ui">Returning now</b> on its late panel: press it when the renter says they are on the way, and they get no more overdue reminders for that return time.</p><p class="gd-p">The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner&#39;s car are on the owner&#39;s page and the car&#39;s page, under <b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>. Open a form, press <b class="gd-ui">Change a value</b>, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under <b class="gd-ui">Versions</b> with their downloads. <b class="gd-ui">Back to the records</b> undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. <b class="gd-ui">Make again</b> keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Discard the values changed by hand</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>, opens the forms&#39; mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under <b class="gd-ui">Earlier mappings</b>. Only the boxes are filled: the form&#39;s own text and layout never change. The owner signs each form on screen: the page shows <b class="gd-ui">Owner&#39;s signature</b> beside the form (who, when, the version) and <b class="gd-ui">Download the print-ready form</b> has no signature on it. A value changed after signing shows <b class="gd-ui">Changed since signed</b> and the owner is asked to sign again.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-close-ended-trips" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Close ended trips</h2><p class="gd-p">A back-dated close sends the renter no email or text. Fleet gets a To do when a trip is still open 2 hours after its return time, and the morning digest lists how many are open.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Field jobs</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Close ended trips</b>: tick the trips that ended and were never closed, mark them returned on time or late (with the time), choose the deposit decision (deduct the balance owed, deduct the late fee, or release in full) and press <b class="gd-ui">Close</b>. An expired card hold is settled by expiry at once. An Admin presses Release for the rest. On a booking, an expired hold after the return has <b class="gd-ui">Mark settled (released by expiry)</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-field-applicant-calls-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Field applicant calls (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Field applicants who pass the AI interview book a 10-minute live call in the hour before the weekly townhall. <b class="gd-ui">Field applicant calls</b> on your home page lists the six slots and who took each one.</p></section>');
-- GUIDES 2130 END
